\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  View: Dollar Seen Staying Strong Ahead Of GDP Data \b0\par\par\uc2 1,192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2000\par 01:00\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- With no key data expected before Thursday, the dollar is likely to continue on its current trend through most of the week, grinding higher against the yen and the euro. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is "going to be fairly volatile, and the focus will be on data here in the U.S.," said Kathleen Stephansen, senior economist at Donaldson, Lufkin & Jenrette. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, first-quarter reports on U.S. advance gross domestic product and the employment economic index are due out. Both are expected to show strong growth. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be making a decision on euro-zone interest rates the same day. A rate hike could provide some temporary support to the sagging single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to analysts. \par \par \uc2  Growing speculation over a Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may help the euro and the dollar against the yen as well. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has timed past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  near holidays to take advantage of thin markets, and Japanese officials have indicated that they are willing to step in to prevent the yen from growing much stronger. European markets are closed Monday for Easter-related holidays. \par \par \uc2  Despite the prospect of an ECB rate hike or BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say the euro stands to lose more ground this week after slipping to new lows against the dollar last Wednesday and Thursday. Traders say the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could test $0.9000 after reaching a nadir of $0.9355 last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders see the dollar keeping rangebound against the yen, with a possible downside risk due to U.S. stock market volatility. \par \par \uc2  "I see dollar/yen hovering around current levels, with tug of war between stock market and the data," said Stephansen. \par \par \uc2  Most financial markets in the U.S. and Europe were closed Friday for the Easter holiday, but the dollar was trading at Y105.82 late Friday, up from Y105.62 early in the New York session and Y105.69 late Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9385, up from $0.9376 earlier and $0.9371 late Thursday. Against the yen, it was buying Y99.23, up from Y99.07 earlier and Y99.04 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Margaret Kudarauska, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at IFR Forexwatch, said technicals indicate an uptrend to around Y106.00-Y106.20, but she sees trading in a range of Y104.50-Y106.50. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the market is all that bullish, but the charts are," she said. \par \par \uc2  Strong U.S. retail sales figures for March have raised economist's forecasts for first-quarter GDP by as much as 1.5 percentage points, with estimates coming in between 4.5% and 6.5%. \par \par \uc2  While a deceleration from 1999 fourth-quarter GDP of 7.3%, a figure anywhere near the 5.7% GDP of the third quarter would indicate that the U.S. economy has shown little inclination to slow down. \par \par \uc2  Coupled with a high employment cost index, the data is likely to add pressure for a further tightening of monetary policy by the Fed at its May 16 meeting. \par \par \uc2  "These items in themselves imply that the dollar should do better, but we'll have to see how the stock market will react. I think the stock market is sitting on pins and needles, worried about higher (U.S.) interest rates," said Sung Won Sohn, chief economist at Wells Fargo Bank in Minneapolis. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. stock market tanked April 14 after an unexpectedly high consumer price index for March raised fears of a hike in U.S. interest rates, and the market has been volatile ever since. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar has been largely unfazed by the U.S. stock market volatility because of coresponding movements in Japan and the major bourses in Europe. \par \par \uc2  "The gyrations in stocks are more within \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regions, so you won't necessarily have downward momentum in the dollar," said Stephansen. \par \par \uc2  The euro, in particular, has failed to capitalize on U.S. stock weakness, so it is unlikely to profit much from further losses in U.S. equities, said Sohn. \par \par \uc2  Allison Montgomery, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at the New York analytical research firm IDEAglobal.com, said the hawkish tone adopted lately by euro-zone officials prompted her to call for a more than 50% chance of a 25 basis point rate hike at the ECB's meeting on Thursday \par \par \uc2  But a rate hike by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not provide much relief for the euro, considering the Fed's tightening trend. The 6% Fed funds rate is already much higher than the 3.5% refinancing rate of the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Stephansen blames the euro's inability to gain against the dollar on growth and interest rate differentials between the U.S. and the euro zone. "As long as we continue to see a growth differential, it's difficult to imagine a correction in the euro. We need to see signs of deceleration in the U.S." \par \par \uc2  However, if the ECB doesn't raise rates Thursday, said Sohn, "the euro could tank." \par \par \uc2  "The ECB is caught between a rock and a hard place," he said. "Inflation's a concern, given the weak euro, so they may may want to raise interest rates." \par \par \uc2  Kudarauska agreed that the euro's new lows have put the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a difficult position. \par \par \uc2  "They don't want to appear to be raising rates to support the euro, and that's the only thing that will make them wait until May," she said. \par \par \uc2  Kudarauska thinks the ECB may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the euro instead. \par \par \uc2  "They've talked about the euro's potential to go up and how the fundamentals are getting better," she said. "If they really believe that, they have to put their money where their mouth is and say, `We're going to stop this."' \par \par \uc2  Kudarauska said traders who were betting on the euro to slip to 90 cents were "playing with fire" because of the threat of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there's all that much downside. It's riskier at this point to bet that it will go below 90 cents than to stabilize," she said. "I think they'll start running into danger on the approach to $0.9000 or $0.9200. That will make the ECB nervous." \par \par \uc2  She sees the euro staying in the 95 cent to 98 cent range in the medium term. \par \par \uc2  But since the ECB has shown little interest in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , help is more likely to come from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where monetary officials have expressed repeated concern over the weakening euro. \par \par \uc2  "I think they (the Bank of Japan) might actually follow through this time around. When it gets down to Y97.50, they will probably get nervous," said Sohn. The euro's low against the yen is Y97.50. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ is usually more focused on dollar/yen levels, however, which\par rose late last week in part for fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The euro also\par strengthened against the yen late last week, reducing the need for an\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par -By Tom Barkley; Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385;\par  tom.barkley@dowjones.com\par -0-\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1141 4137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010805dw4n002ad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
