\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro just above life lows in slow U.S. trade. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2000\par 15:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 21 (Reuters) - Hanging just above record lows, the euro traded unchanged against the dollar and modestly higher against the yen in holiday-thinned activity on Friday as traders braced for fresh losses next week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   traded at 93.73 cents, off 0.04 percent from Thursday's New York closing rate of 93.77 cents and very close to the record low of 93.54 cents set this week.\par Against the yen, the euro\tab      rose 0.48 overnight to stand at 99.23 yen after closing Thursday's session at 98.76 yen, not far above that record low of 97.45 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "People are simply not buying the euro. Investors have given up for the time being and are just eager to stop the pain they have been feeling for so long," said Paul Podolsky, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at FleetBoston in Boston. \par \par \uc2  In the 15 months since 11 European nations adopted the euro, it has lost more than 1/5 of its value against the dollar as growth in Europe still trails America's buoyant expansion and dealers doubt that European leaders can help the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Trading is quiet today. But next week, when the market is running back at normal speed and the U.S. releases new strong growth data, the euro will likely drop further, perhaps testing the 93 cents and then 92.50 cents levels," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. government will release its first look at how quickly the economy grew in the first quarter on Thursday. Wall Street economists expect the gross domestic national product to have grown at a 5.9 percent per year rate, marking a slowdown from the fourth quarter growth but remaining very robust. \par \par \uc2  European markets as well as U.S. stock and bond markets were shut for the Easter holiday but there was some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in the United States. \par \par \uc2  The euro came under fresh pressure this week after the world's leading industrialised nations failed to mention it specifically after a meeting in Washington, suggesting official indifference to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plight. \par \par \uc2  Later in the week, political tensions in Italy sparked by Prime Minister Massimo D'Alema's resignation and calls by Austria's far-right leader for the nation to quit the European Union helped accelerate the selling. \par \par \uc2  While there is some chance that central banks may try to stop the euro's fall by buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market, analysts thought this is unlikely in the face of European leaders' generally unworried demeanor. \par \par \uc2  Only Japan seems appears more concerned, worried that the ongoing strong rise in the yen could harm the nation's fragile recovery. Officials have repeatedly warned they would take action to stop extremely volatile market movements and overnight Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan's top financial diplomat said the euro's recent weakness is not justified by economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "The odds that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  are greater than the odds for the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act, but these odds are still below 50 percent," Podolsky said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile the dollar traded modestly firmer against the yen\tab   at 105.82, hanging above support at 105.40 yen and below resistance at 106 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar rally overnight was spearheaded by a few major hedge funds which speculated that U.S. credit rating agency Moody's Investors Service might soon downgrade Japan's Aa1 debt rating, after having put it on review about two months ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4l020bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
