\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sickly euro trapped near record lows. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2000\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 20 (Reuters) - The euro was weak across the board on Thursday, holding near record lows against the dollar set a day earlier with few prospects of any upturn in sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Concerns of political turmoil in Italy, after Prime Minister Massimo D'Alema resigned on Wednesday, and warnings from Austria's far-right leader Joerg Haider that the country should consider quitting the European Union added to the negative tone. \par \par \uc2  The euro was within a 1/2 cent of record lows it set on Wednesday just below $0.9360. It has lost more than 21 percent from highs hit just after its January 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  However, with a long weekend holiday for Easter coming up in most major financial markets, analysts were unsure how much lower the euro would push near term. \par \par \uc2  "The bias is clearly negative for the euro across the board," said Jesper Dannesboe, treasury economist at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  "The question is whether we can get a follow through today or whether we will get a bit of consolitdaion as we go into the holiday." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the euro's inability to benefit from the breakdown in U.S. equities earlier this week, suggested there was little prospect of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turning higher anytime soon. \par \par \uc2  They said U.S. stocks would still be a focus for the market despite some de-coupling between moves in equities and euro/dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq composite closed 2.3 percent lower on Wednesday and the Dow Jones industrials average was down 0.86 percent, trimming gains made on Monday and Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The only thing which would push euro higher is broadly based sell-off in equities. In the absence of that we will see euro drift lower," said Adam Cole, global economist at HSBC Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  MARKET WARY OF \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Analysts said the threat of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might deter the market from dragging the euro too much lower against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading within one yen of its 97.45 record low set at the end of March. \par \par \uc2  Reports that Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said the euro is too weak in view of European economic fundamentals had markets wary about any moves by the BOJ, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa also put the market on warning saying he had indicated to the rest of the G7 at last weekend's meeting that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "(Japanese) authorities are clearly worried about the euro," said a senior dealer at a major Japanese city bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "After setting a new low overnight, euro/dollar is now on a downtrend. Authorities can step into the market through euro/yen, but it is more likely that they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar/yen while taking into account the levels in euro/yen." \par \par \uc2  Persistent euro bearishness, deriving partly from the lack of coordination among European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) officials, is seen pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below its record low against the yen of 97.55 in the near future, heading south to 90 yen after that, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market is less concerned about action by the ECB after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke's rejection of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a possibility earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  "There's a feeling that if the euro slides through 98.00 yen, the BOJ could step in via dollar/yen, and that's even if the dollar's steady," said a European bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, dollar/yen was broadly steady on the day, trading around 104.80. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said would-be yen bulls were given a pause for thought by speculation Moody's might soon announce the result of its review of Japan's debt rating. This followed news Moody's managing director of sovereign risk Vincent Truglia will visit Tokyo next week and speak at the Foreign Correspondent's Club. \par \par \uc2  Japan's rating was placed under review for possible downgrade on February 17 and since such reviews typically take between two and three months, speculation has been heating up that the announcement could come at any time. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4k01ysa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
