\par\par \b \uc2  Euro clings above new low, BOJ seen hovering. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ayumi Moriyama \par \uc2 874 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2000\par 08:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 20 (Reuters) - The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  clung above record lows in Tokyo on Thursday, propped up only by the prospect of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as players wound down to minimise risks ahead of the Easter holidays. \par \par \uc2  The battered euro stood at $0.9407/12 in quiet afternoon trade, having plunged to a new lifetime low at $0.9359 in New York or $0.9357 on the electronic brokerage system, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  A lack of fresh incentives prevented excessive volatility, but dealers said all eyes were fixed on the performance of U.S. stocks later in the day after a worrying dip on Wednesday following a two-day recovery from last week's heavy losses. \par \par \uc2  The market feared that weakness in the euro against the greenback was likely to spread into euro/yen, which in turn would weigh on the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  But the Easter holidays on Friday and Monday at most major financial centres were prompting the market to avoid holding short positions, as a thin market could trigger disorderly moves. \par \par \uc2  The euro was hanging on at 98.43/52 yen having ended at 98.36 in New York. The dollar was holding steady at 104.63/68 yen against 104.75 in the U.S. Dealers reported good bids around 104.20 yen but heavy Japanese and U.S. offers from 105.15 upwards. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said would-be yen bulls were given pause by speculation Moody's might soon announce the result of its review of Japan's debt rating. This followed news Moody's managing director of sovereign risk Vincent Truglia will visit Tokyo next week and speak at the Foreign Correspondent's Club. \par \par \uc2  Japan's rating was placed under review for possible downgrade on February 17 and since such reviews typically take between two and three months, speculation has been heating up that the announcement could come at any time. \par \par \uc2  Reports that Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said the euro is too weak in view of European economic fundamentals had markets wary about any moves by the BOJ, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa also put the market on warning saying he had indicated to the rest of the G7 at last weekend's meeting that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "(Japanese) authorities are clearly worried about the euro," said a senior dealer at a major Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  "After setting a new low overnight, euro/dollar is now on a downtrend. Authorities can step into the market through euro/yen, but it is more likely that they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar/yen while taking into account the levels in euro/yen." \par \par \uc2  Persistent euro bearishness, deriving partly from the lack of coordination among European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) officials, is seen pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below its record low against the yen of 97.55 in the near future, heading south to 90 yen after that, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market is less concerned about action by the ECB after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke's rejection of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a possibility earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  "There's a feeling that if the euro slides through 98.00, the BOJ could step in via dollar/yen, and that's even if the dollar's steady," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0617GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab      19 Apr.\par \tab \tab \tab   -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/dlr   0.9409   0.9403   +0.06    -6.56   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Dlr/yen    104.64   104.76   -0.11    +2.38   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/yen   98.46    98.36   +0.10    -4.50   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Dlr/swiss  1.6683   1.6690   -0.04    +4.91   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Stg/dlr    1.5802   1.5815   -0.08    -2.31   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Can/dlr    1.4750   1.4752   -0.01    +2.04   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Aus/dlr    0.5955   0.5952   +0.05    -9.26   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/swiss 1.5702   1.5693   +0.06    -2.08   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/stg   0.5949   0.5937   +0.20    -4.65   0.6239\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8584 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0617GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   19 Apr.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9409   0.9403   +0.06    -6.56   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      104.64   104.76   -0.11    +2.38   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab      98.46    98.36   +0.10    -4.50   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6683   1.6690   -0.04    +4.91   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.