\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro wanes as German Ifo adds to negative tone. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2000\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 18 (Reuters) - The euro was hobbled within about one percent of record lows against the dollar and the yen on Tuesday, after a weaker-than-expected German Ifo survey compounded the already negative tone of the market. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially fell as prospects for the dollar improved following the recovery of U.S. stocks on Monday. Euro/dollar set a seven-week low of $0.9454 earlier on Tuesday and retreated towards that level after the Ifo report was released. \par \par \uc2  The closely-watched west German Ifo business climate index fell to 100.5 in March from 100.9 in February. Economists polled by Reuters had expected the index to rise to 101.3. \par \par \uc2  "The German Ifo survey didn't quite live up to expectations and is one of a series of disappointments for the euro," said Glenn Davies, chief economist at Credit Lyonnais in London. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen dipped to the day's lows of 98.70 after the unexpected fall in the Ifo survey, leaving it 1-1/4 yen away from the record lows hit on March 31. \par \par \uc2  "People were disappointed by the figure," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI in London. \par \par \uc2  "But sentiment on the euro is such that even if we had seen a good Ifo figure - in line with or better than expected - I think people would still have been wary of chasing the euro up." \par \par \uc2  The market largely ignored comments from Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke who said late on Monday that Europe was poised to enter a period of strong growth and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to be alert to inflation dangers as the recovery gathered pace. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Finland Governor Matti Vanhala said on Tuesday the ECB's monetary policy was still very loose and that gradual interest rate increases were better than aggressive moves. \par \par \uc2  Although such comments helped fuel speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates at its meeting next week, analysts said a move was pretty much discounted. \par \par \uc2  "Barring another wobble on the Nasdaq, I can't really see any reason for the euro to go up near term," said Davies at Credit Lyonnais. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq composite rose 6.56 precent on Monday, clawing back more than half of Friday's losses, and the Dow Jones industrials average closed nearly 2.70 percent higher. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the outlook for the dollar remained relatively bullish in the short term with U.S. economic growth continuing and initial suggestions that inflation may be kicking in prompting interest rate expectations to be revised up. \par \par \uc2  YEN FIRMER, BUT WARY OF \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar was pegged just above the day's lows around 104.10 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa on Tuesday said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign exchanges if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were too volatile. Earlier in Tokyo he reiterated that the economy was in a recovery trend and said he was not worried about the prospects for Japan's recovery. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said were it not for the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen would have strengthened further. \par \par \uc2  However, the BOJ was not expected to bail out the euro by acting in euro/yen to curb the yen's industry-crippling strength. \par \par \uc2  "Japan has given up on the euro," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Warburg Dillon Read. "Any Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take place against the dollar and the risk is there but recent history has suggested that they need to see 102 in dollar/yen." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they had not spotted the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges to support the euro, even though the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen more than 20 percent against the dollar and 28 percent against the yen since its January 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  "Without any rescue efforts by the ECB, the euro looks pretty much set to test a fresh lifetime low versus the yen and the dollar within several days," said a trader in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4i026ps\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
