\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Yen advances cautiously, BOJ action feared. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ayumi Moriyama \par \uc2 1,026 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2000\par 05:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 18 (Reuters) - The yen advanced cautiously \par \par \uc2  against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo morning trading on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, amid fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the weak \par \par \uc2  euro and failure of Japanese stocks to rebound. \par \par \uc2      Dealers were bewildered when the dollar suddenly jumped \par \par \uc2  around one yen to 105.15, but the lack of follow-through buying \par \par \uc2  prompted them to dismiss the possibility the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The dollar eased back to 104.43/51 yen by noon in Tokyo, \par \par \uc2  compared with 104.50 yen in late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2      The yen stood at 99.03/13 to the euro, after rising to around \par \par \uc2  98.70 from 99.39 in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2      The market's nervousness is due in part to the weak euro \par \par \uc2  after its failure to maintain gains prompted by Friday's rout in \par \par \uc2  U.S. equities. \par \par \uc2      The battered European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inched up to $0.9487/92 \par \par \uc2  from an early seven-week low of $0.9454 but remained vulnerable \par \par \uc2  after the break of key support at 95 cents. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said a bland recovery in Japanese stocks despite a \par \par \uc2  strong rebound overnight in U.S. share prices left uncertain the \par \par \uc2  outlook for stock markets worldwide, making the dollar \par \par \uc2  unattractive. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei stock average ended the morning down \par \par \uc2  0.55 percent at 18,904.65, after rising 1.17 percent shortly \par \par \uc2  after the open. \par \par \uc2  That compared with the 2.7 percent gain by the Dow Jones \par \par \uc2  industrial average and the biggest one-day points gain ever for \par \par \uc2  the Nasdaq on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the Nikkei remained under pressure \par \par \uc2  after a decision to replace 30 components of the index, mainly \par \par \uc2  companies in "smokestack" industries, with high-tech shares \par \par \uc2  representing Japan's "new economy". \par \par \uc2  The change in the composition of the Nikkei - the main \par \par \uc2  barometer for Japan's share market - continued to trigger heavy \par \par \uc2  selling of the 30 issues to be eliminated. \par \par \uc2  Regarding BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said comments by \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities were in part preventing the yen from gaining \par \par \uc2  at a faster rate. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said Japan \par \par \uc2  was concerned about the strong yen and that it is ready to sell \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market again if necessary. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0306GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   17 Apr.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr   0.9483   0.9522   -0.41    -5.83   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/yen    104.47   104.50   -0.03    +2.21   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen   99.08    99.39   -0.31    -3.90   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss  1.6539   1.6489   +0.30    +4.01   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Stg/dlr    1.5764   1.5798   -0.22    -2.55   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Can/dlr    1.4842   1.4847   -0.03    +2.68   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Aus/dlr    0.5925   0.5911   +0.24    -9.72   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss 1.5688   1.5705   -0.11    -2.17   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg   0.6005   0.6021   -0.27    -3.75   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said a bland recovery in Japanese stocks despite a strong rebound overnight in U.S. share prices left uncertain the outlook for stock markets worldwide, making the dollar unattractive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The benchmark Nikkei stock average\tab    ended the morning down 0.55 percent at 18,904.65, after rising 1.17 percent shortly after the open.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That compared with the 2.7 percent gain by the Dow Jones industrial average and the biggest one-day points gain ever for the Nasdaq on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said the Nikkei remained under pressure after a decision to replace 30 components of the index, mainly companies in "smokestack" industries, with high-tech shares representing Japan's "new economy".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The change in the composition of the Nikkei - the main barometer for Japan's share market - continued to trigger heavy selling of the 30 issues to be eliminated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Regarding BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said comments by Japanese authorities were in part preventing the yen from gaining at a faster rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said Japan was concerned about the strong yen and that it is ready to sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market again if necessary, even though a weekend Group of Seven statement was mum on the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fumihiko Kawano, manager of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  section at Nomura Securities, said the fact that the G7 communique issued last Saturday mentioned a line about major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was still taking a grip on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The statement after the meeting of finance minister and central bankers from the G7 rich club nations in Washington did not refer explicitly to the yen, euro or dollar, saying instead: "Exchange rates among the major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should reflect economic fundamentals."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Kawano also said that looking at the BOJ's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics, they tend to take action when they see an accumulation of speculative yen-long positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ didn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yesterday because they probably decided that the market was not long enough in yen yet. They are waiting for the most effective timing," he said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8550 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0306GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   17 Apr.\par 