\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-BOJ stymies Japan's war against strong yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 776 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2000\par 14:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 12 (Reuters) - Japan may have a new foe in its war against export-damaging yen strength - the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The government has trusted the BOJ to lead the attack on yen bulls in the past 10 months but saw its efforts begin to unravel on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the yen soaring again by indicating its near-zero interest rates may be set to rise. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masura Hayami said conditions were falling into place for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to end its policy of holding rates at rock-bottom lows to foster economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength seems at odds with comments like these which boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But Hayami's comments may be truer to the BOJ's stance than its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market activities, because the latter are conducted only at the behest of the Finance Ministry. \par \par \uc2  As a result of this apparent policy discrepancy, analysts reckon it is unlikely Japan will feel justified in asking other members of the Group of Seven nations, whom it will meet this weekend, to unite against excessive yen strength or volatility. \par \par \uc2  "The timing is appalling," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The G7 has made an explicit commitment to countering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, and here is one of the G7 contributing to volatility just days before they meet. It is also undoing a lot of the good work \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had done on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  G7 SHARES CONCERN \par \par \uc2  The United States, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Germany, France, Britain, Italy, and Canada, who make up the G7, said after their January meeting that they shared Japan's concern about the potential impact of yen appreciation for the Japanese and the world economy. \par \par \uc2  In previous statements they have emphasised their commitment to promoting policies which help avoid excessive volatility or misalignments in exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has sold yen repeatedly on behalf of the Finance Ministry in the past year to curb strength which was hurting exporters and thus threatened Japan's budding economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least 17 times since June 1999 and has made a minimum of four forays into the foreign exchanges so far this year. \par \par \uc2  The monetary policy outlook the BOJ outlined on Tuesday could now see it called on to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to halt the very rally it has triggered, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ does not want to undermine what the MOF is doing but what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is saying reflects the fact that the two institutions have got slightly different priorities," said Malcolm Barr, European economist at Chase Investment Bank. \par \par \uc2  "If the MOF had the call on rates you would never have heard them making such noises on monetary policy. But the general consensus is that we will see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if and when the yen moves with any momentum through 103 against the dollar." \par \par \uc2  The dollar has fallen back to levels around 105 yen from the two-week highs above 107 it was scaling on Tuesday while the euro is back around 100.50 yen from the 103.50 highs it was eyeing only a day ago. \par \par \uc2  BATTLE EVEN HARDER NOW \par \par \uc2  But if Japan thought fighting the $1.5-trillion-a-day foreign exchanges was tough before, it could find the battle even harder now that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders have scented differences between policymakers. \par \par \uc2  "It seems a bit perverse as they are undermining everything they have been doing," said the chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "People have been left a bit confused and the pressure on the yen is on the upside once more." \par \par \uc2  There was little sign of any let-up in demand to buy yen for dollars and euros, particularly after Belgian Finance Minister Didier Reynders made it clear on Tuesday the euro zone did not want any help from the G7 in bolstering the euro. \par \par \uc2  A renewed push towards the record lows around 97.50 yen which the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  set at the end of March was expected to give the yen added impetus to rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But with the latest bout of yen gains of Japan's own making, the Japanese government's fight to keep the yen down was expected to remain a lonely one. \par \par \uc2  "The yen had begun to weaken and everything was calming down and it was the perfect backdrop to the G7 - and now it has all been shattered by Japan's own actions," said Parsons at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4c02j8g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
