\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar hits 1-week high vs yen, but gain slows. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 864 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2000\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 10 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped to a week-high \par \par \uc2  above 106 yen in Tokyo on Monday morning, partly on safe-haven \par \par \uc2  buying prompted by North Korea saying it would make an "extremely \par \par \uc2  important broadcast". \par \par \uc2      "The market was on alert for what the North Korean would say, \par \par \uc2  and started buying dollars," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2      But the fears proved unfounded. Pyongyang announced that \par \par \uc2  South Korean President Kim Dae-jung will meet North Korea's \par \par \uc2  reclusive leader Kim Jong-il June 12-14 for an historic summit \par \par \uc2  between the two countries which remain technically in a state of \par \par \uc2  war. The news slowed the dollar's gain. \par \par \uc2      Substantial buy offers from Japanese exporters should also \par \par \uc2  keep a lid on the dollar's upside, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      With the dollar trading above 106 yen, exporters using \par \par \uc2  forwards can lock in conversion rates for their \par \par \uc2  dollar-denominated revenue above their planned exchange rate for \par \par \uc2  this financial year. A recent Bank of Japan (BOJ) survey found \par \par \uc2  major manufacturers budgeted an average exchange rate of 104.36 \par \par \uc2  yen for the year begun April 1. \par \par \uc2      Around midday in Tokyo, the dollar was trading at 106.08/13 \par \par \uc2  yen, up from 105.36 yen in late U.S. trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the dollar is likely to hold its gains for the \par \par \uc2  short-term as the market is very cautious of dollar-buying \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a Group of \par \par \uc2  Seven meeting on Saturday in Washington. \par \par \uc2  The market has started speculating Japan will try to convince \par \par \uc2  other industrialised nations to reiterate concern about an \par \par \uc2  excessive yen rise. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's Policy Board is meeting on Monday, but the market \par \par \uc2  expects no surprise, as it fears even a hint of tightening could \par \par \uc2  send the yen even higher ahead of a G7 meeting this weekend. \par \par \uc2  Following the dollar's gain against the yen, the European \par \par \uc2  single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also shot higher versus the yen, topping 101.20, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      That in turn helped the euro bounce from $0.9535 to $0.9555 \par \par \uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      The euro had slid against the dollar after European finance \par \par \uc2  ministers and central bankers said they would not seek a \par \par \uc2  supportive statement for their ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the G7 meeting \par \par \uc2  this weekend. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0256 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   07 Apr.\par \tab \tab \tab      --------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr   0.9551   0.9547   +0.04    -5.15   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/yen    106.00   105.36   +0.61    +3.71   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen   101.23   100.57   +0.66    -1.81   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss  1.6448   1.6431   +0.10    +3.43   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Stg/dlr    1.5793   1.5789   +0.03    -2.37   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Can/dlr    1.4574   1.4579   -0.03    +0.82   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Aus/dlr    0.5970   0.5980   -0.17    -9.04   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss 1.5707   1.5695   +0.08    -2.05   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg   0.6039   0.6047   -0.13    -3.21   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the offers on the upside, dealers said the dollar is likely to hold its gains for the short-term, as the market is now very cautious of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's (BOJ) dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of the Group of Seven meeting on Saturday in Washington.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market has started speculating Japan will try to convince other industrialised nations to reiterate concern about an excessive yen rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ's Policy Board is meeting on Monday, but the market expects no surprise, as it fears even a hint of tightening could send the yen even higher ahead of a G7 meeting this weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers also detected dollar-buying from investment trusts, prompted by the start of the new financial year on April 1.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is the second week of the new fiscal year, so it's about time to see some investment overseas," a city bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Following the dollar's gain against the yen, the European single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      also shot higher versus yen, triggering heavy stop-loss buying through 100.75 to reach above 101.20 in a sharp short squeeze, dealers said.\par That in turn helped the euro bounce from $0.9535\tab   to $0.9555 against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro had slid against the dollar after European finance ministers and central bankers said they would not seek a supportive statement for their ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the G7 meeting this weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, Japanese finance ministry data released this morning showed that Japanese investors sold a net 150.1 billion yen of foreign bonds and 225.1 billion yen of foreign stocks in March. Japanese stock buying by foreign investors slowed in March, totalling a net 14.1 billion yen, down from a net increase of 859.6 billion yen in February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Total net monthly outflow from Japanese assets was 104.8 billion yen in March, which was far below that of previous two months. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8478 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4a02ro8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
