\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Watch: Officials Cast Doubt On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 's Value \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum \par \uc2 910 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2000\par 02:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- A recent Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  report suggests that yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted on a massive scale just Monday, might ultimately cause the yen to shoot up even higher. \par \par \uc2  In a report last month, officials Takeshi Kimura and Kou Nakayama wrote that the yen has been the most volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  among those of the leading industrialized nations over the last twenty years, partly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets. \par \par \uc2  On average since the 1980's, the effective yen rate has been about 30% to 50% more volatile than the dollar and pound, and around 100% more volatile than the Deutsche mark and French franc, the officials wrote. The effective rate is a weighted average of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its counterparts. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, the yen has a peculiar tendency to become more volatile when it strengthens. This in turn tends to accelerate its appreciation, the two say. One reason is that exporters rush to cut \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses when the yen rises. Another is that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , paradoxically, causes the yen to rise again once the immediate impact fades. \par \par \uc2  "The government has tended more to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the appreciation of the yen than to weaken it, but when such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't change the sentiment of market participants, it could be that volatility was heightened as the market was pushed forcefully into the weaker yen zone," they wrote. \par \par \uc2  Because the yen tends to strengthen even more rapidly when it becomes volatile, that implies that yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ironically caused a stronger yen down the line. \par \par \uc2  Private analysts say their experience bears those observations out. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities, more than their U.S. and European counterparts, "have tended to try to move the market by force with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than relying on fundamentals" to determine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, says Takashi Yamanaka, economist at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That's only caused "energy to accumulate" for the yen to spring back\par up, he adds.\par -\par    Some Have Seen Rift Between BOJ, MOF\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two officials say their opinions don't represent the BOJ's\par official view, and it's highly unlikely that they were attempting to\par criticize Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, which is molded by the\par Finance Ministry. Their report is a sober, scholarly analysis of the\par effect of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility on Japanese exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But some have speculated in the past that there's a rift between MOF\par and BOJ on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, and one argument the BOJ was believed to\par espouse was that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is often ultimately useless, if not\par outright counterproductive. As \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy recovers and the BOJ\par inches toward raising interest rates, there will inevitably be upward\par pressure on the yen: if traders feel the two institutions are at\par loggerheads over the need for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they might be tempted to\par push the yen up even more.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Just Monday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market again,\par selling by some estimates more than $10 billion worth of the Japanese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop a yen rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There's little reason to believe that the BOJ was opposed to that\par round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the yen rise that preceded the BOJ action was\par sharp, with the dollar dropping four yen to Y102.06 on the Friday before\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Top BOJ officials have repeatedly warned against sharp\par moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The fall also brought the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par perilously close to psychological support at Y100.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even if the BOJ was opposed to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, it wouldn't make\par any difference - MOF calls the shots on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  just follows orders.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last summer, that arrangement peeved some within the BOJ.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Eisuke Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs at\par the time, was orchestrating an ultimately futile effort to keep the\par dollar above Y120 by selling tens of billions of dollars worth of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. Some BOJ officials felt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a\par useless exercise.\par -\par    Some Say BOJ Powerless To Thwart Yen Rise\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In some ways, there are even more incentives now to bid up the yen now\par than a year earlier: the economy is recovering, the domestic stock\par market is buoyant while Wall Street is unstable, and there are growing\par signs that the BOJ is serious about raising rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Tuesday, for example, BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said if personal\par consumption recovers firmly, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could begin considering\par abandoning its zero interest rate policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Therefore, it's widely believed in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market that the dollar\par will eventually fall below Y100.00, even if authorities try to prevent\par that from happening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Such a fall could genuinely hurt the economy: large manufacturers\par predicted in the last BOJ Tankan survey that the dollar-yen would trade\par at Y104.36 this fiscal year, and if it falls too much below that level,\par it could sour corporate sentiment and cut into profits, dragging down\par the economy as a whole.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But some analysts say that artificially pushing down the yen poses\par risks of its own: it keeps afloat exporters that might be better left to\par sink, delaying structural reform of the economy, for example.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Monetary authorities are ignoring the negative impact of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Their stance is that if things are all right now,\par everything is fine," says Ryohei Muramatsu, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at\par Commerzbank in Tokyo.\par     -By Kenneth McCallum; 813-5255-2938; ken.mccallum@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1042 4131 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4701t6p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
