\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar struggles,but market fears BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 930 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2000\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 6 (Reuters) - The dollar was trading a bit below 105 yen in Tokyo on Thursday morning, struggling to hold its value amid lingering jitters over U.S. share markets. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback was supported by a market obsessed by possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen strengthens sharply, endangering Japan's economic recovery by reducing the value of Japanese companies' overseas earnings and adding to deflationary pressure within the domestic economy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 104.77/80 yen by late morning, down from 104.90 at the U.S. close on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little changed at $0.9616/26 against $0.9621 in late U.S. trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was confined to tight ranges throughout the morning, holding firmly above its overnight low of around 104.70 yen. Overseas fund operators and Japanese exporters showed strong selling interest above 105.20 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The Tokyo market has been really quiet recently. Many dealers and speculators here have been sidelined, especially since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday," a U.S. bank dealer said. "We'll see some direction in the dollar/yen rate after U.S. jobs data (on Friday)." \par \par \uc2  The dealer said that uncertainty in the U.S. share markets and persisting prospects of convincing economic recovery in Japan were factors encouraging yen-buying. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, the dollar was being supported by buying by Japanese institutional investors. Japanese pension funds and asset management firms are buying dollars to invest in foreign bonds in the new fiscal year which began this month. \par \par \uc2  The euro held above $0.96 in Tokyo on speculation the Group of Seven finance ministers may take a tougher stance on the soft euro when they meet April 15 in Washington, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Sirkka Hamalainen's comments on Wednesday also helped the euro by reminding markets that the ECB is ready to react if inflation pressures persist and the euro's value does not reflect economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, ECB President Wim Duisenberg said in an Italian newspaper interview on Wednesday that the euro was stable, not weak, around the 95-cent level and would realise its potential in the wake of a strong economic recovery in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at 100.80/88 yen little changed from a U.S. close of 100.86 on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0254 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %\par \tab \tab \tab \tab      05 Apr.\par \tab \tab \tab   ------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/dlr   0.9620   0.9621   -0.01    -4.47   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Dlr/yen    104.89   104.90   -0.01    +2.62   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/yen   100.89   100.86   +0.03    -2.14   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Dlr/swiss  1.6377   1.6361   +0.10    +2.99   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Stg/dlr    1.5853   1.5831   +0.14    -2.00   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Can/dlr    1.4506   1.4501   +0.03    +0.35   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Aus/dlr    0.6062   0.6058   +0.07    -7.63   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/swiss 1.5759   1.5749   +0.06    -1.73   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/stg   0.6074   0.6070   +0.07    -2.64   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro held above $0.96 in Tokyo on speculation the Group of Seven finance ministers may take a tougher stance on the soft euro when they meet April 15 in Washington, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Sirkka Hamalainen's comments on Wednesday also helped the euro by reminding markets that the ECB is ready to react if inflation pressures persist and the euro's value does not reflect economic fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, ECB President Wim Duisenberg said in an Italian newspaper interview on Wednesday that the euro was stable, not weak, around the 95-cent level and would realise its potential in the wake of a strong economic recovery in the euro zone.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo dealers said the euro will be supported but its gains will be limited as many U.S. fund operators are looking to sell euros at $0.9650 to $0.97.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said on Thursday that the euro was too weak given economic fundamentals and that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements should reflect fundamentals, but dealers said the market showed a muted reaction to his remarks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro was quoted at 100.80/88 yen\tab     , little changed from a U.S. close of 100.86 on Wednesday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0254 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg