\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Slips Vs Yen As Exporters Hedge \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nick Shindo \par \uc2 833 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2000\par 07:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar glided lower against the yen in Asian trading Thursday despite a tumble in the Nikkei stock average as local exporters sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for hedging purposes. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell slightly against both the dollar and the yen after sentiment took a light hit from the news that the planned mega-merger between Deutsche and Dresdner banks had broken down. \par \par \uc2  Near to a 200 point dive in the Nikkei by Thursday afternoon failed to deliver a boost to the dollar against the yen. Following the uninspiring pattern of the last two sessions, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to hop out of a tightly traded band, locked in by support around Y104.70 and offers attributed to Japanese exporters and local trust banks just above Y105.00, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In addition to the lasting impact of Monday's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dollar buying demand from investment trusts looking to divert local capital into U.S. treasuries provided added support to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters have reportedly been active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards market in recent days as part of their new fiscal year hedging activities, capping the dollar's upside just above current levels, they said. \par \par \uc2  Jitters from the recent volatile moves in U.S. stock prices is also discouraging investors to go long on dollars, others noted. \par \par \uc2  "It's a very tight market, with the dollar's upside capped by the recent shakes in U.S. stocks," said Hidenori Watanabe, assistant general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank. \par \par \uc2  In the absence of major trading incentives Thursday a reputed expiry of a large Y105.00 option later in the session helped to keep the dollar pinned down to that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y104.91, just below Y105.08 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.45 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9624, down from $0.9637 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9636 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y100.97, down from Y101.27 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y101.61 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  With the dollar continuing to trade comfortably below its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -bolstered high of Y105.62 on Monday, signs are that market fears of renewed BOJ action at current levels are dissipating somewhat, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are diminishing a bit, but people are still cautious during Tokyo hours," said Koichi Udagawa, assistant manager of the treasury and securities division at Daiwa Bank. "But it's likely that the dollar will get sold down a little further when trading shifts overseas," he added. \par \par \uc2  Looking further ahead, the dollar should be able to garner some support from several quarters in the weeks to come. \par \par \uc2  Japanese pension fund dollar buying is expected to kick off next week as fund managers actively reposition assets as part of new fiscal year investment plans here, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In addition, yen bullish sentiment is expected to be tamed as the financial heads of the Group of Seven leading industrial nations meet next week in Washington. The G7 members are expected to repeat concern about the potentially damaging economic impact of an excessively strong yen rate, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Reaffirmation of the BOJ's zero-interest rate policy at the meeting will do little to attract new money to the yen either, they said. \par \par \uc2  More importantly, traders will be keeping a close eye on any verbal or written support for the embattled euro at the upcoming meeting. \par \par \uc2  Although the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to stick to its guns about the euro's upside potential, if no concern about further weakening is officially expressed by the G7, the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could quickly slide to new lows against both the yen and the dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  If the G7 adopts a hands off approach to the euro, expect a drastic reaction in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, said DKB's Watanabe. \par \par \uc2  "If the communique doesn't include a mention of concern towards excessive euro weakness then the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will plummet again," he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite arguments from some analysts that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is vastly undervalued and will eventually rise as a matter of course, "it still needs propping up," Watanabe added. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5865, up from $1.5840 in New York but lower than $1.5950 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nick Shindo; 813-5255-2929; nick.shindo@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On T