\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar vulnerable vs euro, wary of U.S. stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2000\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 5 (Reuters) - The dollar was soft against the euro on Wednesday but had recovered much of its poise after a choppy previous session on the back of gyrations in U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro largely ignored higher than expected German jobless data, instead finding support from comments made by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  member Sirkka Hamalainen who reminded the market that the ECB was ready to react if inflation pressures persist. \par \par \uc2  Hamalainen also said that euro-zone interest rates were still low and that the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value did not reflect economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading around a cent below Tuesday's one-week highs around $0.9750, after the high-tech Nasdaq composite index recovered to the close from intra-day losses of more than 13 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody knows that the euro-zone economy is recovering and the key to the turnaround in the euro over the last day or two has been the volatility in U.S. stocks," said Patrick O'Sullivan, economist at AIB Group Treasury in Dublin. \par \par \uc2  Blue chip stocks also recovered most of their losses, with the Dow Jones industrials average ending 0.42 pct lower after falling four percent earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  "If we were to see a broad-based correction in U.S. stocks, then we would see the dollar under pressure, but I don't see this happening at the moment," said Adam Cole, European economist at HSBC Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  O'Sullivan at AIB said Hamalainen's comments and strong Eruopean services sector indices had bolstered the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Hamalainen gave reference to the idea that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still a weapon within the ECB armoury if they feel that the euro weakness was to get exacerbated and that is giving some support," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro-zone March services activity index rose above the consensus forecast to 60.9, matching its record high set in October 1999. \par \par \uc2  The euro shrugged off a report that the pan-German jobless rate declined less than expected to 10.6 percent in March from 10.9 percent in February, focusing instead on equity markets. \par \par \uc2  "The German unemployment numbers weren't terrific, but that has been dismissed in favour of the longer term progression of the euro-zone economy as a whole which is going to be quite healthy and will be supportive for the euro," O'Sullivan said. \par \par \uc2  SWISS FRANC STRENGTH CONTINUES \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc, meanwhile, proved the main beneficiary of safe haven flows out of the dollar, reversing early weakness to 1.64 francs against the dollar. It was testing its lows for the day in the mid-1.62 area, around 1-1/2 centimes off five-week highs set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro/Swiss franc exchange rate was approaching its record lows around 1.57 francs set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Strength in the Swiss franc was initially triggered after Swiss National Bank Chief Economist Georg Rich made it clear on Monday that the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was no longer trying to hold the franc stable against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the yen was broadly steady against the dollar, more than three yen above last week's three-month lows set before Monday's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there was little reaction in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to the election of Yoshiro Mori as Japan's new prime minister on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Mori reappointed the cabinet who had resigned en masse on Tuesday after Former Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi fell into a coma upon suffering a stroke over the weekend, and no changes in economic policy were expected. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar remained within sight of the previous day's 18-month lows of US$0.60, despite a quarter-point rise in the official cash rate to 5.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of Australia ascribed a large part of the rate hike to weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but analysts were surprised by the RBA's hawkish commentary and the extent of the discussion of recent Australian dollar weakness, and its inflationary implications. ((London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4503153\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
