\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar calms vs euro after stock-led storm. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2000\par 10:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 5 (Reuters) - The dollar stabilised against the euro on Wednesday following a roller-coaster ride in the previous session chasing U.S. stock prices. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded nearly 1-1/2 cents below Tuesday's one-week highs around $0.9750 after the high-tech Nasdaq composite index recovered to the close from intra-day losses of more than 13 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the resilience of the Dow Jones industrial average and "old economy" stocks underpinned the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "If we were to see a broad-based correction in U.S. stocks, then we would see the dollar under pressure, but I don't see this happening at the moment," said Adam Cole, European economist at HSBC Markets in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the Group of Seven nations would help support the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, gave the euro some support, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers pondered speculation that the Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors may include a reference to the euro at the G7 meeting on April 15. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. may be more worried about the euro's weakness. But it still seems European officials are indifferent over taking specific action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," a dealer at a Japanese bank in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg reinforced this view on Wednesday, saying in an Italian newspaper interview that the euro was not weak at $0.9550, but was stable. \par \par \uc2  The euro shrugged off a report that the pan-German jobless rate rose to a larger-than-expected 10.6 percent in March, focusing instead on equity markets. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc, meanwhile, proved the main beneficiary of safe haven flows out of the dollar, although it weakened to around 1.64 francs to the dollar on Wednesday, from five-week highs around 1.61 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro/Swiss franc exchange rate remained within half a centime of record lows around 1.57 francs set on Tuesday, after Swiss National Bank Chief Economist Georg Rich made it clear this week the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was no longer trying to hold the franc stable against the euro. \par \par \uc2  YEN STABLE, IGNORES POLITICS \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 105 yen, more than three yen above last week's three-month lows set before Monday's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen was showing little reaction to the election of Yoshiro Mori as Japan's new prime minister on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Former Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi's cabinet resigned on masse on Tuesday after Obuchi fell into a coma upon suffering a stroke over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  "Worries over the dollar are emerging and the fallout from the stock market has mostly affected euro/dollar. It's difficult to buy yen (against dollar) after Monday's (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at a U.S. bank in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, appetite for yen from overseas investors is expected to remain intact on expectations for Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  But the BOJ's recent dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely temper yen-buying interest in the short run, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar remained within sight of the previous day's 18-month lows of US$0.60, despite a quarter-point rise in the official cash rate to 5.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of Australia ascribed a large part of the rate hike to weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but analysts were surprised by the RBA's hawkish commentary and the extent of the discussion of recent Australian dollar weakness, and its inflationary implications. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw45030h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
