\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar recovers from Nasdaq shock, yen soft. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2000\par 14:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 4 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed against the yen on Tuesday amid political uncertainty in Japan and trimmed early losses against the euro as the initial impact of Monday's selloff in U.S. technology stocks faded. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was underpinned against the yen as ailing Japanese Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi was expected to be replaced as early as Wednesday and as yen bulls were tamed by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ has sent quite a clear message yesterday, and also there's a number of political uncertainties generated by the fact that the prime minister is in a coma," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar had initially weakened broadly after Monday's 7.64-percent drop in the Nasdaq composite\tab   , the bastion of the technology-fuelled "new economy" in the United States, after an antitrust ruling against Microsoft Corp .\par Yet, Nasdaq 100 index futures\tab   traded on the 24-hour electronic system, GLOBEX2, bounced back on Tuesday, highlighting the resilience of U.S. markets, traders said.\par They also noted that the broader U.S. stock market had gained on Monday, with the Dow Jones industrial average\tab   rising 2.75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's too early to say that the dollar is on a weaker footing, particularly as people are just rotating into the Dow," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dollar\tab   was little changed from Monday's close, drifting near the middle of the day's tight $0.9520-0.9570 range, while dollar/yen\tab   hovered near the top of the day's 104.90-105.70 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders noted that the euro had yet to shake off its independent weakness of late - it barely moved after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said on Tuesday he was convinced the euro would strengthen soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par YEN BULLS STYMIED BY BOJ, OBUCHI ILLNESS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They added that the dollar's only weakness had been against the buoyant yen, which this week has been steadied by the BOJ's huge yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is still very eager to buy the yen, but can't really do so after seeing the BOJ's heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yesterday," a Tokyo-based trust bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders estimated the BOJ might have spent well over $10 billion in Monday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For now, many traders were just sitting on the sidelines, keeping an eye on the political development in Tokyo and shifting their focus to a Group of Seven meeting of finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chiefs in Washington on April 15.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Tokyo, the entire cabinet of Prime Minister Obuchi, who is still in a coma after suffering a stroke at the weekend, resigned in a step toward forming a new government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ruling Liberal Democratic Party Secretary-General Yoshiro Mori, a seasoned politician with broad support in the party, was expected to become LDP president and to be voted in as prime minister by parliament on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the most part, traders expected little yen reaction to such a changeover, particularly as Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa is likely to be reappointed in the new cabinet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "All it does is that it changes the election timing. The election timing might change but I don't think it will have a radical impact in what's happening in Japan," said Michael Lewis, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  economist at Deutsche Bank in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculation is rife that the LDP would call an early general election, perhaps before the Okinawa Group of Eight Summit in July, given compassion votes expected in wake of Obuchi's misfortune. Such votes gave the party a landslide victory in 1980 after the death of then-Prime Minister Masayoshi Ohira.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw44036q4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
