\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen retreats on BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , Obuchi. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 1,004 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2000\par 08:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 3 (Reuters) - The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled nearly three yen against the dollar on Monday as a determined Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) tirelessly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a surge in the yen in overseas trading. \par \par \uc2  News that Japanese Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi had suffered a stroke and was in intensive care also weighed on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But yen sentiment remained bright on hopes for Japan's economic recovery, underscored by an overall improvement in the BOJ's closely watched March "tankan" survey of corporate sentiment released on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Perhaps because of the focus on the tankan the BOJ decided to come in at this stage and force a correction. But long term we see a yen strengthening bias, so it's not sustainable," David Harvey, general manager of investment strategy at IBJ, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was quoted at 104.97/5.00 yen\tab   after hitting a three-month low of 102.03 yen in overseas trade on Friday. It closed at 102.75 yen in U.S. trade on Friday.\par The euro was also boosted against the yen\tab     , rising to 100.57 yen after hitting a lifetime low of 97.55 yen in overseas trade on Friday. The euro was at 98.20 yen in late U.S. trade on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ, which acts as the government's agent for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , repeatedly bought dollars, starting from around 103.30 yen and pushing the greenback to a high of 105.65 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MOF) confirmed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We responded at a good point," Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa told reporters outside his office. "Volatility is troubling and we are responding firmly."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ appeared to start selling yen at around the 103 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Looking at the way the dollar has jumped, it seems that the BOJ initially stepped in from around the low end of the 103 to 104 yen range," shortly after the release of the tankan survey, a commercial bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued buying dollars above 105 yen, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ aimed to show a very strong stance about curbing the yen's rise," another bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely did not involve euro-buying, yen-selling action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese life insurers were detected bidding for dollars on dips.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But many dealers were doubtful whether large capital outflows from Japanese investors would materialise to push up the dollar against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Even though the new fiscal year has started, I don't think we can expect the kind of capital outflows from Japanese investors as we have seen in the past," a third dealer at a major city bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In fact, some investors were building dollar-short, yen-long positions as soon as trade for the new fiscal year kicked off," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Selling interest remained steady from Japanese exporters, dealers added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the BOJ's tankan survey, the key diffusion index for large manufacturers came in at minus nine, just a touch better than median market forecasts of minus 10, and businesses saw only a modest further improvement to minus five in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But analysts detected signs of strength from the survey, particularly in investment and profits.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The index for capital spending by large manufacturers swung to a healthy rise of 4.9 percent, the first positive result since 1995, while all firms were predicting profit growth of over 15 percent for the coming year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and growing political uncertainty in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may put a dampener on the recent yen-buying mood, but it would be a short respite.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the Japanese authorities drop their stance of stemming the yen's rise, it would easily shoot above 100 yen (to the dollar)," the third bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts also said political uncertainty will not likely have a sustained impact on the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taisuke Tanaka, director and strategist for global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Credit Suisse First Boston, said: "Obuchi's hospitalisation may raise political turmoil. But the market was not expecting additional macroeconomic policies from the Obuchi government right now," so the impact on the yen should be limited. The markets' stance was illustrated by the rise in Tokyo share prices, he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The benchmark Nikkei stock average closed up 1.92 percent, or 389.67 points, at 20,726.99 on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers also cited some wariness ahead of the meeting of Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors on April 15.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the MOF's International Bureau, told reporters on Monday that he did not know whether the Group of Seven industrialised nations would discuss coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the G7 meet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But chances for coordinated action itself seemed slim.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par When asked about the euro's fall on Friday, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Wim Duisenberg said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was only an option if the fall harmed monetary policy and admitted there was very little the bank could do. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0625 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   31 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9518   0.9560   -0.44    -5.48   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      104.93   102.75   +2.12    +2.66   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab      99.82    98.20   +1.65    -3.18   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6693   1.6645   +0.29    +4.97   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5890   1.5916   -0.16    -1.77   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4500   1.4486   +0.10    +0.31   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6066   0.6073   -0.12    -7.57   0.6