\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen bruised after assault by Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2000\par 14:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Adds estimates of size of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in paragraph 7 and quotes in paragraphs 17-18, updates prices.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 3 (Reuters) - The yen was beaten back on Monday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to the runaway rally it staged at the end of last week. \par \par \uc2  It was at least the fourth time this year that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb export-damaging yen strength and came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied four percent on Friday to hit record highs against the euro and three-month peaks against the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and news that Japanese Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi was in a coma after suffering a stroke forced the yen to give up more than half of the ground it had conquered on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But it was expected to resume its rally before long as Japan's closely-watched "tankan" survey of Japanese business sentiment reinforced optimism about the country's economy on the first trading day of the new Japanese fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has worked for today but the underlying tone is still yen bullish," said Mark Cliffe, chief economist at ING Barings in London. \par \par \uc2  "People are taking the view that the signs of recovery we are seeing in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are yen bullish and barring any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the U.S., \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will just be attempting to stem the tide." \par \par \uc2  BOJ UNLEASHES YEN SELLING \par \par \uc2  The BOJ repeatedly bought dollars for yen in Tokyo on Monday, starting from around 103.30 yen shortly after the release of the tankan report. Market sources in Japan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have bought more than $10 billion on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the dollar as high as 105.60 yen, up from Friday's three-month lows around 102. The euro rallied on its coat tails, climbing to peaks above 100.50 compared with the record lows around 97.50 yen it plumbed on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The speed of the yen's gains on Friday had made \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  inevitable and the foreign exchanges were braced for more such action in the days ahead, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "It was always on the cards after the moves we got on Friday and I am just kicking myself for not having bought down there," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "I would not be surprised to see them \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if we got more upward pressure on the yen." \par \par \uc2  But Japan was expected to struggle to keep the yen down for too long as long as the United States and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  The yen had already clawed its way back to around 105 per dollar and 100 per euro by the European midsession. \par \par \uc2  Even Obuchi's illness was not expected to contain demand for yen for too long as cabinet members said they would press on with his economic stimulus policies. \par \par \uc2  Confidence this would be the case allowed Japan's Nikkei stock average close nearly two percent higher on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility and the bullish outlook for the Nikkei were seen limiting capital outflow from Japan in the new fiscal year that began on April 1. \par \par \uc2  Paul Chertkow, head of global research at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London, said that the euro's past weakness against the yen would also deter Japanese investors from taking their money overseas. \par \par \uc2  "There may be some people who looking at opportunities to put money abroad because of the strength of the yen but the amount is likely to be limited and domestic investors are likely to put increasing amounts of money into the equity market in Japan," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro has lost as much as 26 percent of its value against the yen since its January 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  A slew of strong purchasing managers' reports from Germany, France, Italy, and for the whole of the 11-nation euro zone bolstered the euro against the dollar as they showed the manufacturing sector expanding at its fastest pace in the surveys' history. \par \par \uc2  However, this proved of fleeting interest to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers who were fixated on moves in the yen. The euro was therefore left holding broadly steady above $0.95. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw43030oj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
