\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen dented, BOJ fears cast long shadow. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2000\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 3 (Reuters) - The yen was beaten back on Monday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to the runaway rally it staged at the end of last week. \par \par \uc2  It was at least the fourth time this year that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb export-damaging yen strength and came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied four percent on Friday to hit record highs against the euro and three-month peaks against the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and news that Japanese Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi had suffered a stroke at the weekend forced the yen to give up more than half of the ground it had conquered on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But it was expected to resume its rally before long as Japan's closely-watched "tankan" survey of Japanese business sentiment reinforced optimism about the country's economy. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has worked for today but the underlying tone is still yen bullish," said Mark Cliffe, chief economist at ING Barings in London. \par \par \uc2  "People are taking the view that the signs of recovery we are seeing in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are yen bullish and barring any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the U.S., \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will just be attempting to stem the tide." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WAS ON THE CARDS \par \par \uc2  The BOJ repeatedly bought dollars for yen in Tokyo on Monday, starting from around 103.30 yen shortly after the release of the tankan report. \par \par \uc2  Its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the dollar as high as 105.65 yen, up from Friday's three-month lows around 102. The euro rallied on its coattails, climbing as far as 100.53 compared with the record lows around 97.50 yen it plumbed on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The speed of the yen's gains on Friday had made \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  well nigh inevitable and the foreign exchanges were braced for more such action in the days ahead, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "It was always on the cards after the moves we got on Friday and I am just kicking myself for not having bought down there," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "I would not be surprised to see them \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if we got more upward pressure on the yen." \par \par \uc2  But Japan was expected to struggle to keep the yen down for too long as long as the United States and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  Even Obuchi's illness was not expected to contain demand for yen for too long. \par \par \uc2  Taisuke Tanaka, director and strategist for global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Credit Suisse First Boston in Tokyo, said the market had not been expecting any additional macroeconomic policies from the Obuchi government at the moment. \par \par \uc2  "The markets' stance was illustrated by the rise in Tokyo share prices," he added. The Tokyo stock market's Nikkei average closed up 1.92 percent at 20,726.99 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility and the bullish outlook for the Nikkei were seen limiting the expected seasonal capital outflow from Japan due to Japanese institutions' asset allocation for the new fiscal year that began on April 1. \par \par \uc2  "The big question is whether we will see the traditional capital outflow from Japan in the new fiscal year as this would be the only substantial point in the dollar's favour against the yen," said Cliffe at ING. \par \par \uc2  The euro/dollar market was sidelined amid all the yen action, hovering slightly above $0.95. \par \par \uc2  A slew of stronger-than-expected purchasing managers' reports from Germany, France, Italy, and for the whole of the 11-nation euro zone bolstered the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but proved of fleeting interest to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw43030oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
