\par\par \b \uc2  Yen gains vs dollar, euro but BOJ fears loom. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ayumi Moriyama \par \uc2 860 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 30 (Reuters) - The yen pushed higher against the dollar and euro on Thursday afternoon aided by bullish comments from Fed board member William McDonough, but fell short of a rally amid worries of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The New York Fed President's words caused the dollar to instantly drop 0.20 yen to around 105.40 yen and the euro to fall 0.25 yen to about 100.45 yen, reflecting the market's will to bet for a further advance of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Talking to businesspeople in Tokyo, McDonough expressed great optimism about Japan's economic prospects saying he predicted a "Japanese economic miracle". \par \par \uc2  He said his confidence was shared by sophisticated U.S. investors who told him that they were "absolutely euphoric" about Japan's outlook based on its embrace of new technologies and restructuring of old industries. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the euro, McDonough said the current exchange level of the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  posed no problem from an economic perspective, and added that movements in the dollar against the yen were no threat for the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  "McDonough's words gave momentum to the yen, but the market is very nervous about the possibility of BOJ (yen-selling) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this time of the day," said a Japanese trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which tumbled to a four-week low of 105.00 yen overnight was quoted at 105.61/62 yen by 0617 GMT against 105.69 yen in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 100.56/76 yen after dropping to a record low of 100.02 yen overnight and compared with 100.66 yen in late U.S. trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro was quoted at $0.9526/35, up from $0.9514 in late New York trade. \par \par \uc2  Yen-buying overnight was partly from European fund managers moving to boost investment in Japanese equities. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may rise near crucial levels of 100.00 yen for euro/yen and 105.00 yen for dollar/yen, where stop-loss sell orders and knockout option triggers are said to lurk. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's stock market closed lower on Thursday for the first time in five sessions, as nervous investors locked in profits after its recent rapid advance. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Nikkei average\tab    of 225 leading shares closed down 265.15 points or 1.28 percent at 20,441.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although there were no signs of yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday, Finance Ministry officials reiterated their intent to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to blunt the yen's advance if necessary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy is recovering gradually, and given the difference in interest rates between Japan and the United States, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should reflect (economic) fundamentals," Vice Finance Minister for international affairs Haruhiko Kuroda told reporters. He added that Japan will take action in the market if needed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ conducts \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of the ministry.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders, however, said chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during European or U.S. trading hours were slim, since it seemed unlikely that either the U.S. Fed or the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would give the BOJ a hand to suppress the yen's advance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the ECB is expected at Thursday's policy-setting meeting to leave interest rates unchanged, judging from recent dovish comments by ECB officials as well as positive developments on inflation, such as the benign IG Metall pay settlement and OPEC's agreement to boost oil production.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the Japanese economy, speculation that next week's BOJ "tankan" business sentiment survey will provide further evidence of an improvement in Japan's economy underpinned the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's natural for the yen to be bought since hopes for a recovery in the Japanese economy are rising," said Ryohei Muramatsu, manager of treasury and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Commerzbank in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But traders said that for now, the market is driven by options-related moves rather than fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Investors have been mostly sidelined ahead of the fiscal year-end in Japan and the end of the first quarter in the United States," a city bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0646GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   29 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9532   0.95