\par\par \b \uc2  OUTLOOK-Reuters Asia Business at 0530 GMT. \b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 07:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      Following are some of the main business news stories (all \par \par \uc2  times GMT) \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      MARKETS \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE/LONDON/FRANKFURT - Key Asian markets fall on \par \par \uc2  jitters as another tumble on Nasdaq reflected concerns over \par \par \uc2  sky-high valuations of tech stocks. The yen eases against the \par \par \uc2  euro and steady versus the dollar as yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the Japanese unit from adding to \par \par \uc2  its overnight gains. \par \par \uc2      ** Wraps of major regional market moves \par \par \uc2      OIL PRICES FALL ON OPEC \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE - U.S. crude futures extended falls in Asia as \par \par \uc2  the market digested OPEC's deal to raise production. \par \par \uc2      ** From SINGAPORE/LONDON/NEW YORK fresh market updates \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      WTO CHINA EU TALKS \par \par \uc2      BEIJING - European Union Trade Commissioner Pascal Lamy and \par \par \uc2  Chinese counterparts begin a third day of talks on China's WTO \par \par \uc2  entry with pressure mounting on both sides to hammer out a \par \par \uc2  deal. Expect: \par \par \uc2      ** New story including expected start of talks, comments \par \par \uc2  from Lamy, comments from WTO head Moore in Brussels \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      JAPAN-USA TELECOMS \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - In a sign of mounting tension in a U.S.-Japan trade \par \par \uc2  spat, U.S. Ambassador to Japan Thomas Foley was set to meet \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's telecommunications minister to press for sharp cuts in \par \par \uc2  rates charged by telecoms giant NTT. \par \par \uc2      ** Fresh story and end of day wrap \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      FED'S MCDONOUGH SEES IMBALANCES IN U.S. ECONOMY \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - Federal Reserve Bank of New York President William \par \par \uc2  McDonough says he sees signs of imbalances and strains in the \par \par \uc2  U.S. economy, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rate hikes \par \par \uc2  were having little effect. \par \par \uc2      ** Update \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      JAPAN SOFTBANK \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - Japan's Softbank Corp, which has suffered a \par \par \uc2  stunning share price fall of more than 50 percent in just six \par \par \uc2  weeks, may face a bumpy road to rekindle the appetite of \par \par \uc2  investors, with doubts growing over its Internet "zaibatsu" \par \par \uc2  strategy, analysts say. \par \par \uc2      ** Outlook on Softbank internet plans \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      JAPAN BANKING TAX \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - Tokyo Metropolitan assembly expected to enact a \par \par \uc2  controversial law slapping a new tax on big banks amid signs \par \par \uc2  other local authorities may do the same. \par \par \uc2      ** Story after passage expected around 0530 \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      JAPAN SONY-SAKURA-J.P.MORGAN INTERNET BANK \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - Japan's Sony Corp to unveil an online banking \par \par \uc2  alliance with J.P. Morgan and Sakura Bank to give the \par \par \uc2  electronics giant gain a more solid footing in the financial \par \par \uc2  sector and win a banking licence. \par \par \uc2      ** Update after 0500 news conference \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      KOREA BANK REFORMS SET TO PICK UP \par \par \uc2      SEOUL - The pace of South Korea's bank reform is set to \par \par \uc2  pick up this year with the government prodding mergers, but \par \par \uc2  analysts said consolidation was not an answer to removing bad \par \par \uc2  banks.     ** Analysis \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE TELECOMS LIBERALISATION \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE - Singapore flings open doors to its coveted \par \par \uc2  telecoms sector to leapfrog Asian competitors as the regional \par \par \uc2  base for IT players, drawing $1.75 billion in investments over \par \par \uc2  the next three years. \par \par \uc2      ** Story on issuing of new licences ahead of the opening on \par \par \uc2  April 1 and impact on Singapore Telecommunications. \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      MALAYSIA RINGGIT PEG \par \par \uc2      KUALA LUMPUR - Malaysia is sticking to its undervalued \par \par \uc2  exchange rate but analysts say time is ripe for authorities to \par \par \uc2  adjust the 19-month-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg. \par \par \uc2      ** Analysis of the ringgit peg and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  monetary policies. \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      JAPAN CATTLE DISEASE FEARS \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - Japan orders all fodder straw from China and South \par \par \uc2  Korea disinfected as it races to find the source of a suspected \par \par \uc2  outbreak of foot-and-mouth disease that could even hit its \par \par \uc2  fabled Kobe beef industry. \par \par \uc2      ** New story \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      STRUGGLING THAI BANKS SEEN AVOIDING MERGERS \par \par \uc2      BANGKOK - Thai banks will struggle for a few more years to \par \par \uc2  recover from massive bad loans run up during the Asian economic \par \par \uc2  crisis but are strong enough to survive alone for a while and \par \par \uc2  resist being taken over by foreign banks. \par \par \uc2      ** Outlook for Thai banks \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      If you have any queries, please call: \par \par \uc2  