\par\par \b \uc2  Yen blunted by BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 936 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 30 (Reuters) - The yen was easier against the \par \par \uc2  euro and steady against the dollar in late morning trading on \par \par \uc2  Thursday, as wariness of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the yen from adding to its overnight gains. \par \par \uc2      The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose overnight to a record high of \par \par \uc2  100.02 yeb against the euro and a four-week high of 105.00 yen \par \par \uc2  against the dollar, partly due to yen buying by European fund \par \par \uc2  managers moving to boost investment in Japanese equities. \par \par \uc2      "It's natural for the yen to be bought since hopes for a \par \par \uc2  recovery in the Japanese economy are rising," said Ryohei \par \par \uc2  Muramatsu, manager of treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \par \par \uc2  Commerzbank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2      Speculation that next week's BOJ "tankan" business survey \par \par \uc2  will provide further evidence of an improvement in Japan's \par \par \uc2  economy underpinned the yen. \par \par \uc2      Although there were no signs of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \par \par \uc2  the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Ministry officials reiterated their \par \par \uc2  intent to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to blunt the yen's advance if necessary. \par \par \uc2      "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy is recovering gradually, and given the \par \par \uc2  difference in interest rates between Japan and the United States, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reflect (economic) fundamentals," Vice \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister for international affairs Haruhiko Kuroda told \par \par \uc2  reporters. He added Japan will take action in the market if \par \par \uc2  needed. \par \par \uc2   The euro was trading at 100.76/84 yen late Thursday morning \par \par \uc2  in Tokyo, against 100.66 yen in late U.S. trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      The dollar stood at 105.68/72 yen against 105.69 yen in late \par \par \uc2  U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2      Against the dollar, the euro was quoted at $0.9533/38, up \par \par \uc2  from $0.9514 in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also unlikely to get any support from a meeting \par \par \uc2  of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governing council in Madrid later \par \par \uc2  in the day. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll of 22 economists in Europe and North America \par \par \uc2  showed that none of them expected ECB to raise interest rates on \par \par \uc2  Thursday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0259 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   29 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr   0.9536   0.9514   +0.23    -5.30   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/yen    105.59   105.69   -0.09    +3.31   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen   100.72   100.66   +0.06    -2.31   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss  1.6709   1.6755   -0.27    +5.07   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Stg/dlr    1.5923   1.5922   +0.01    -1.56   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Can/dlr    1.4568   1.4563   +0.03    +0.78   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Aus/dlr    0.6113   0.6113   +0.00    -6.86   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss 1.5943   1.5935   +0.05    -0.58   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg   0.5985   0.5960   +0.42    -4.07   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the dollar, the euro was quoted at $0.9533/38 as of 0254 GMT, up from $0.9514 in late U.S. trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the chances for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may rise near crucial levels of 100.00 yen for euro/yen and 105.00 yen for dollar/yen, where stop-loss sell orders and knockout option triggers are said to lurk.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer for a European bank said the yen could try for those levels in the near term, especially since the market had been caught off guard by signs of a fund inflow to Japan from Europe.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dealer said the market had recently been focusing more on the amount of foreign investment by Japanese investors from April, when a new business year starts, rather than capital inflows to Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "At the most, what you heard was that Japanese investors were unlikely to invest very aggressively overseas," said the dealer for a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But now there is a lot of talk about potential capital flows (from Europe), which has scared market players, although they can't really see the actual flows," said the dealer for a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Besides talk of European investors' interest in Japanese stocks, DaimlerChrysler AG's recent decision to take a 34 percent stake in Mitsubishi Motors Corp has pressured the euro against the yen, dealers said. The euro was also unlikely to get any support from a meeting of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governing council in Madrid later in the day, with a news conference scheduled at 1230 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll of 22 economists in Europe and North America showed that none of them expected ECB to raise interest rates on Thursday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0259 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   29 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9536   0.9514   +0.23    -5.30   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      105.59   105.69   -0.09    +3.31   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     100.72   100.66   +0.06    -2.31   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6709   1.6755   -0.27    +5.07   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5923   1.5922   +0.01    -1.56   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4568   1.4563   +0.03    +0.78   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6113   0.6113   +0.00    -6.86   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.5943   1.5935   +0.05    -0.58   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.5985   0.5960   +0.42    -4.07   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3u03fbb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
