\par\par \b \uc2  Euro gyrates after ECB leaves rates unchanged. \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 30 (Reuters) - The euro fell towards its record lows against the yen after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left rates unchanged on Thursday but swiftly rebounded amid wariness \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be launched in its support. \par \par \uc2  Analysts polled by Reuters had unanimously expected rates to be left on hold but traders who had deferred selling euros on the off chance the ECB could spring a surprise began to offload the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it announced its decision. \par \par \uc2  This drove the euro down as low as 100.06 yen, within a hair's breadth of the record lows it set on Wednesday, and to $0.9537. \par \par \uc2  However, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly recouped its losses. \par \par \uc2  "There's been a bit of euro/yen selling on the back of the ECB no change announcement but when somebody bought it at the lows the market got nervous about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But it is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  A resurgence in optimism about the Japanese economy and broad-based gloom about the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prospects have driven the euro down about 4.5 percent against the yen so far this week. \par \par \uc2  Traders have also been encouraged to drive the euro lower against the yen in absence of any Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's industry-crippling strength in recent days and as traders bet the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not step in to halt the euro's fall. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was most recently spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling yen on the foreign exchanges on March 15. It has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least 16 times since June 1999. \par \par \uc2  Traders are now seen waiting for the ECB's news conference which is scheduled for 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3u03c91\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
