\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED -  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro up after ECB holds rates steady. \b0\par\par\uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 18:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In NEW YORK story headlined "\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Euro up after ECB holds \par \par \uc2  rates steady" please read in 19th paragraph "...after the \par \par \uc2  muscular IG Metall industrial union..." instead of "...after \par \par \uc2  the muscular UG Metall industrial union..." (correcting typo). \par \par \uc2  A corrected repeat follows. \par \par \uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 30 (Reuters) - The euro found breathing room above all-time lows against the yen and day lows against the dollar in New York trade on Thursday after Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates steady and gave no signs it would act to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the euro's gains were temporary as traders \par \par \uc2  took some profits after three days of steady declines. \par \par \uc2  "This is just a little short covering rally but there will be levels to sell again," said John McCarthy, vice president at ING Barings. "I still think we'll see a lower euro over time." \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had few surprises for the market when it decided to hold its key refinancing rate steady at 3.50 percent and its president, Wim Duisenberg, said the ECB would remain vigilant to counter inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg reaffirmed that the beleaguered euro was undervalued and did not reflect improving European economic growth prospects. But he said there was "not much more" the ECB could do to lift the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think the ECB is aware that it is not going to help their cause to continue to raise rates just for the sake of the euro, nor to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2  The ECB last raised its refinancing rate by 0.25 percent on March 16, but with the U.S. Federal Reserve also in a monetary tightening cycle, interest rate changes have had little net impact on the euro. \par \par \uc2  A stronger than expected reading for U.S. fourth quarter growth, released by the Commerce Department on Thursday morning, had little impact on the market but underscored the blistering pace of the economy which has prompted the Fed to tighten policy. \par \par \uc2  Gross domestic product was revised up to an annual rate of 7.3 percent compared to 5.7 percent in 1999's third quarter.     The euro tested life lows against the resurgent Japanese yen near 100 yen before bouncing to the 100.90 area as the market stood on guard for potential Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb export-crippling yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also clawed back some ground after dipping to a two-week low against the yen overnight on renewed enthusiasm that Japan's sluggish economy is on the road to recovery. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that the Bank of Japan will deliver a strong quarterly "tankan" survey of business sentiment on Monday have bolstered the yen. \par \par \uc2  Comments overnight by the U.S. Federal Reserve's William McDonough fanned the fires of a stronger yen when he predicted a "Japanese economic miracle." \par \par \uc2  While BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears helped buoy the euro above the 100 level, dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be at risk of falling into double-digits and trigger a wave of stop-loss selling in New York. \par \par \uc2  "I think New York is the most likely time zone for euro/yen to go under 100. I think the other two time zones seem to have more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns than the U.S.," said Ben Strauss, vice president at Bank Julius Baer. \par \par \uc2  Tracking its performance against the yen, the euro briefly dipped to overnight lows against the dollar near 95.10 cents before ticking back near 95.90 cents in early New York trade.     While the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held above Wednesday's one-month low of 94.76 cents, dealers said it was unlikely to generate much momentum. \par \par \uc2  "I think people are quite bearish on the euro. No ECB rate hike, while expected, is probably the decision we will see every two weeks for the next month or two," Gilmore said.     He said prospects for lower oil prices after OPEC's output deal this week and German wage restraint after the muscular IG Metall industrial union accepted a moderate regional wage deal this week should help keep euro zone inflation in check.     ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, +212 859-1660)) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:18 p.m. (1518 GMT).  All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\tab \tab \tab     Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %   1999\par 29 Mar.\tab \tab \tab Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab  0.9587   0.9514   +0.77   -4.80   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab   105.26   105.69   -0.41   +2.98   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab  100.91   100.66   +0.25   -2.12   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab 1.6608   1.6755   -0.88   +4.44   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab   1.5937   1.5922   +0.09   -1.48   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab   1.4576   1.4563   +0.09   +0.84   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab   0.6111   0.6113   -0.03   -6.89   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab