\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -BOJ nerves stifle yen gains against euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 30 (Reuters) - The yen traded a little below the previous session's record highs against the euro on Thursday, as fear of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tempered enthusiasm about the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to all-time troughs around 100 yen on Wednesday after strong Japanese output data fanned hopes of recovery in the world's second largest economy. \par \par \uc2  The data raised expectations of a strong quarterly "tankan" survey of business sentiment, to be released on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "All this talk about Japanese economic recovery seems a little previous, and the authorities do not want to see the yen strengthening, but the market is looking for a good tankan report," said Glenn Davies, chief economist at Credit Lyonnais in London. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Federal Reserve board member William McDonough expressed great optimism about Japan's economic prospects earlier on Thursday in Tokyo, saying he predicted a "Japanese economic miracle". \par \par \uc2  Analysts said persistent yen repatriation flows ahead of the end of Japan's fiscal year on March 31 had also been bolstering the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last few weeks. \par \par \uc2  But fears of further market action by the BOJ stemmed the euro's fall, and the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered to 100.60 by 0930 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "There is definitely a risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Adam Cole, global economist at HSBC Markets in London. "The fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be an important factor putting the stop underneath the euro against the yen. But if euro/yen downward pressure is related to the end of the fiscal year (in Japan), there is a really small window in which they (BOJ) need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was trading a little above 105, where traders said fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and talk of large options positions supported the dollar. \par \par \uc2  NO CHANGE SEEN FROM ECB \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar, which had tumbled to a one-month low of $0.9476 on Wednesday on the back of euro/yen's plunge, regained more than a cent and was hovering around $0.9560, ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fortnightly policy-setting meeting. \par \par \uc2  All 22 economists polled by Reuters this week forecast no change to the ECB's 3.50 percent refinancing rate. \par \par \uc2  "It's extremely unlikely we will see any rate change today, but at the press conference they may talk about the impact on inflation of the weak euro," said Davies. \par \par \uc2  The ECB's rate decision is expected at 1145 GMT, and a news conference starts at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  News that industry sources said hedge fund Tiger Management LLC will close its flagship Jaguar fund to stem losses from ill-timed stock picks added to nervousness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, although dealers said it was hard to predict the possible impact of the news. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair which may have been affected was the Swiss/yen exchange rate, which could have suffered from the unwinding of leveraged yen carry trades, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "When you look at what has happened to the Swiss franc in the last week, with the Swiss raising interest rates, it is surprising Swiss/yen is so low," said a dealer from a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Switzerland raised the target range for the three-month London interbank offered rate (LIBOR) by 75 basis points on March 23, to 2.50-3.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc was trading around 63 yen at 0940 GMT, just over half a yen above multi-year lows of 62.40 yen set on March 14. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3u03bj6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
