\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro jittery as ECB leaves rates steady. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Updates with ECB rate decision, fresh quotes, latest prices) \par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 30 (Reuters) - The euro eyed record lows before bouncing against the yen on Thursday, in jittery trade after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed expectations and left interest rates unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell towards record lows against yen and sterling and a one-month low against the dollar set in the previous session, as the ECB left its key refinancing rate at 3.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  The ECB raised the refi rate by 25 basis points at its previous meeting on March 16. \par \par \uc2  Although steady rates were generally expected, traders who had deferred selling euros on the off-chance of a surprise rate hike began to sell after the rate decision. \par \par \uc2  "Selling was postponed until after the meeting because people did not want to take even the small risk of them doing something," said Jesper Dannesboe, treasury economist at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro then jumped around a third of a yen from lows near 100, in a market wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb industry-crippling yen strength. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen dipped to two-week lows below 105, a key level for options positions, traders said, and was trading just below that level by 1210 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that the Bank of Japan will deliver a strong quarterly "tankan" survey of business sentiment on Monday were adding to yen gains and so increasing the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Persistent yen repatriation flows ahead of the end of Japan's fiscal year on March 31 had also been bolstering the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last few weeks, analysts added. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Federal Reserve board member William McDonough fanned the fires of a stronger yen earlier on Thursday, saying in Tokyo he predicted a "Japanese economic miracle". \par \par \uc2  ECB MAY DISCUSS WEAK EURO \par \par \uc2  Attention, meanwhile, was turning to the ECB's news conference following its policy-setting meeting, due to start at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "At the press conference they may talk about the impact on inflation of the weak euro," said Glenn Davies, chief economist at Credit Lyonnais in London. "That means the exchange rate could have a second round effect on inflation and interest rates." \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar, which had tumbled to a one-month low of $0.9476 on Wednesday on the back of euro/yen's plunge, regained nearly one cent on Thursday and was hovering around $0.9550. \par \par \uc2  News that industry sources said hedge fund Tiger Management LLC will close its flagship Jaguar fund to stem losses from ill-timed stock picks added to nervousness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, although dealers said it was hard to predict the possible impact of the news. \par \par \uc2  The fund was likely to have already unwound any loss-making \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3u03946\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
