\par\par \b \uc2  Japan most likely defender of sagging euro/yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 13:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the most likely major industrial power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges in response to the euro's fall to new record lows against the yen this week, analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The solo campaign Japan has waged against yen strength in the past nine months has been motivated by the tangible damage such gains inflict on Japanese exporters and the country's budding economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Wariness Japan could soon unleash another wave of yen selling was therefore rife after the euro fell to within a hair's breadth of 100 yen on Wednesday, down 25 percent since its 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  Broad euro weakness has played its part in fanning inflation in the euro zone but the impact on public confidence has been just as often mentioned by policymakers in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  While the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may want to stop the rot, analysts said this would be a bad time for its first foray into the foreign exchanges given traders were more inclined to test their resolve than buy the theory that the euro had turned. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the only really likely candidate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if we are going to get any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (on euro/yen), but it is not a great time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Brian Kiely, treasury technical strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland in London. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only works in changing the market's mind when the market is having second thoughts anyway - it doesn't look like this is the case at the moment." \par \par \uc2  JAPAN FIGHTS ALONE \par \par \uc2  A European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  working paper published in February said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign exchanges can successfully influence exchange rates, particularly when authorities act in concert and relatively infrequently. \par \par \uc2  Japan does not fit the bill given traders have spotted it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen at least 16 times since June 1999. Also, it has fought a lonely battle so far, though it has used the Fed and the ECB as a conduit for its yen sales on occasion. \par \par \uc2  While this may explain why the yen's rally has proved indefatigable, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  racking up gains of nearly 20 percent against the euro and 13 percent against the dollar since the Bank of Japan's first sortie into the market last year. \par \par \uc2  But Japan's success should be measured against the aims of its authorities, which may have been more modest, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ means it is the marginal buyer of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at a time when the private sector in Japan is keeping its money at home," said Paul Lambert, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  "This means that the yen is at a weaker level than it would otherwise have been, all other things being equal." \par \par \uc2  Any ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would definitely have the element of surprise and increase the impact of official efforts to weaken the yen against the euro, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But even so, the effect was still expected to be fleeting - A factor which was seen persuading the ECB to keep its powder dry and its dignity intact. \par \par \uc2  "If we go below 100 I would expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the BOJ but not see a strong possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the ECB," said Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas in Paris. \par \par \uc2  "They have realised that there is not a lot to be achieved by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they cannot turn the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around by that method when all the capital flows are going the other way." \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3u0393i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
