par The euro, which had stood around $0.9760 at the start of the week, was quoted at $0.9580/90\tab  , down slightly from $0.9603 in New York late on Tuesday. It briefly dropped to a three-week low of $0.9538 in early trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Expectations of a wider interest rate differential between the euro-zone and the United States was weighing down on the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In a separate Reuters poll, all 55 economists surveyed predicted that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will keep its key interest rate on hold when its governing council meets on Thursday, although 47 predicted a 25 basis point hike in the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers still saw the chance of the U.S. Federal Reserve tightening by another 50 basis points before the end of June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was limited reaction in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to news that the Organisation of Petroleum Exporting Countries, excluding Iran, had agreed to raise oil output by 1.7 million barrels per day. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0234 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   28 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9580   0.9603   -0.24    -4.87   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      106.10   105.79   +0.29    +3.81   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     101.64   101.68   -0.04    -1.42   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6610   1.6554   +0.34    +4.45   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1