\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 -2: Key To Mapping Yen's Course In Hands Of MOF \b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A slew of dollar/yen options expiring Tuesday with strikes between Y106.00-Y107.00 is also helping to contain the dollar's movement, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, however, the market appears almost evenly split over the yen's future course. \par \par \uc2  Some market players believe if next week's tankan survey indicates that the nation's economic recovery is at least partially in the bag, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve to fight further yen strengthening will wane, clearing the way for a rally against both the dollar and euro. \par \par \uc2  "MOF has been the main obstacle blocking further yen gains against the dollar, but signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy is picking up may persuade \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionists\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step aside," said one foreign bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  But a top ministry official remained defiant Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  MOF's international bureau head Zembei Mizoguchi reiterated to Nikkei News that rapid yen strengthening is "undesirable" and won't be tolerated by the Japanese authorities even if the tankan survey presents a case for increasing economic optimism. \par \par \uc2  "Our (\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) stance won't change," he said. \par \par \uc2  In any case, given that Wednesday is the last \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading day for settlement in this fiscal year ending March 31, other dealers expect the dollar to rebound against the yen as Japanese investors pump new capital into overseas assets over the coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, the U.S. economy appears on course for a gentle descent from its recent heady growth rates, and with a sustainable Japanese recovery still not yet confirmed, the yen looks ripe for a gradual near-term decline against the dollar - particularly if BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears are alive, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sanwa's Hashimoto expects the dollar to rise to around Y111.00 next month before stabilizing. \par \par \uc2  "After that, the conventional view in the market is that the dollar will slowly drop back to around Y105.00," but there could be some interim negative shocks - such as a possible Moody's downgrade of Japanese debt - that could jolt the dollar even higher, he said. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the euro ticked up to a high of $0.9690 late in the session on news that Germany's largest trade union I.G. Metall had struck a wage deal with North Rhine Westphalia metal producers. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later fell back on light profit-taking, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5899, up from $1.5866 in New York and higher than $1.5935 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nick Shindo; 813-5255-2929; nick.shindo@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3s01lqc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
