\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Kuroda: Euro Undervalued Vs Yen, Dollar -FT \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 03:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The euro is sharply undervalued versus the yen and the dollar and should rebound soon, Haruhiko Kuroda, Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice minister for international affairs said Wednesday, according to Thursday's international edition of the Financial Times. \par \par \uc2  The FT quoted Kuroda as saying: "The economic fundamentals show that the euro should be much stronger - its weakness does not reflect fundamentals." \par \par \uc2  His remarks echo similar recent comments from Japanese and European officials. \par \par \uc2  Japan's stance towards the euro is likely to be closely watched by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the coming days, in the wake of growing market interest in the attitude of European and Japanese authorities towards the euro's decline, the FT reported. \par \par \uc2  This interest has been partly spurred by a report from Jiji, a Japanese newswire, which claimed earlier this week that France's finance ministry asked \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Mar. 8, the FT reported. \par \par \uc2  On that day, the Bank of Japan bought dollars in Tokyo markets and euros in European markets, carrying out instructions of Japan's finance ministry, the FT reported. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3n01in1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
