\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro trails dlr and yen in popularity stakes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wayne Cole \par \uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 06:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 22 (Reuters) - The euro sagged to two-week lows against the dollar on Wednesday as investors voted with their feet and rushed headlong into U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  Treasury prices rallied to six-months highs and all the major U.S. equity indices racked up solid gains in reaction to a well-flagged 25 basis point hike by the Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  The tightening took rates to their highest level since 1995 and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  clearly warned that more could be needed, but investors celebrated anyway, safe in the belief that the Fed was not out to throttle the economy. \par \par \uc2  That drew the inevitable comparisons with Europe's growth pretensions, which despite more upbeat German data were labelled as second-best by the majority. \par \par \uc2  "It's very much an old economy versus a new economy story," Patrick Bennett, director, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Warburg Dillon Read, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "People want to participate in the structural reform and growth story in the U.S., and while Europe is recovering, it still has very severe structural problems," he said, pointing to Europe's relatively high levels of unemployment. \par \par \uc2  Even Japan was considered more of a restructuring story than Europe, he added. \par \par \uc2  Traders said whatever the rationale, the tide was undeniable with sustained selling first triggering stop-loss sales through support at $0.9690 in New York and then $0.9630 and $0.9600 here in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By late morning the euro\tab   was lying broken at $0.9591 having fallen from $0.9639 late in New York and a high on Tuesday around $0.9735.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts noted the retreat had shattered trendline support and added a technical element to the euro's list of woes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The two-week wedge pattern has been decisively broken to the donwside and this is likely to open a multi-day decline," said analysts at IDEA. Support was seen at $0.9520, a trough from March 8, but most saw it as no more than a stepping stone on the march lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's a chance the move will be as meandering as the recent rally was...but ultimately it's likely to lead to a retest of the (record) $0.9390 low," said IDEA.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The outlook was hardly better against the yen, where the euro had slumped to 102.32 yen\tab      from 103.00 late in New York and a high around 103.80 on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said Japanese exporters still seemed to have cover to take even though most institutional repatriation flows appeared to have dried up now that the March year-end was near.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The flow out of euros and into yen in turn put pressure on the dollar, dragging it to 106.69 yen\tab   from 106.85 in the U.S. and an overnight high around 107.25.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, traders expected Tuesday's low of 106.25 to provide solid support, particularly as the market remained wary of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Lest anyone had forgotten, Finance Ministry \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Haruhiko Kuroda restated the official line that there was no need for the yen to strengthen further given current economic fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was also much interest in a Jiji news agency report released on Tuesday which claimed that the BOJ had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the euro on March 8 at the request of the French Finance Ministry.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This was hastily denied by the French and analysts found it hard to believe France would go behind the back of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ask Japan to support the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But some traders were not so quick to dismiss the story.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We know that the MOF and the French Finance Ministry have quite close links," said a trader at a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We know the French were concerned by the euro's slide, and the ECB wasn't. So is it impossible that the French dropped a hint to the MOF that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in euro/yen might be a good idea? Unlikely maybe, but impossible? No."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If even a part of the tale was true, it would expose deep rifts within the EU11 and the ECB about the management of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with negative implications for the euro. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8584 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0216 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   21 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9593   0.9639   -0.48    -4.74   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      106.74   106.85   -0.10    +4.43   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.37   103.00   -0.61    -0.71   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6802   1.6723   +0.47    +5.66   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5689   1.5726   -0.24    -3.01   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4700   1.4697   +0.02    +1.69   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6081   0.6097   -0.26    -7.34   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6114   1.6116   -0.01    +0.49   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6109   0.6126   -0.28    -2.08   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3m03v2y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
