\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar firms on uncertainty ahead of Taiwan vote. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 985 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 07:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 17 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed slightly against the yen in late Tokyo trade on Friday, supported by growing uncertainties over Taiwan's presidential election. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were worried that tensions between Taiwan and China could escalate depending on the outcome of the poll, to be held on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Such worries prompted safe-haven buying of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Lingering speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to buy dollars for yen ahead of a three-day weekend also lent support to the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The euro was mixed against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to hike key interest rates on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 105.94/6.02 yen compared with 105.50 yen in late U.S. trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9693/98 against $0.9713. Against the yen, the euro was at 102.69/82 yen versus 102.49 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Amid a dearth of incentives in the afternoon, dealers focused on the Taiwan election," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were wary that a victory by pro-independence candidate Chen Shui-bian was likely to heighten tensions with China. \par \par \uc2  Even so, the dollar's gains against yen were limited in Tokyo hours. "There are growing concerns over how China will react, but we can't really factor anything in until the election results are known," the first bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar edged up to a high of 106.10 yen in early trade, buoyed by commercial bids at the 0100 GMT retail fixing due to strong dollar demand ahead of the extended weekend. \par \par \uc2  Japanese financial markets will be closed on Monday for the the Vernal Equinox, a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar was knocked off the 106 yen level by selling from Japanese exporters. Interbank and overseas operators were also detected taking profits. \par \par \uc2  "Short-term operators built long positions near 105.50 yen on expectations of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But when the BOJ failed to emerge, they were happy to lock in profits near 106.00 yen," a dealer at a major city bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's gains against the yen were also limited as Japanese investors converted funds back into yen ahead of book-closings at the end of March. Some dealers said that such seasonal yen-buying interest would continue to support the yen next week. \par \par \uc2  Brighter prospects for the Japanese economy also helped sentiment towards the yen, especially as leading indicators of capital spending such as machinery orders and industrial production are showing gains. \par \par \uc2  A survey by business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun on Friday said capital spending by Japanese manufacturers will grow by 0.5 percent year-on-year in the fiscal year from April 1, the first rise in three years. \par \par \uc2  In an expected move, the Japanese government on Friday upgraded its assessment of the economy, saying movements toward a self-sustaining recovery were gradually appearing. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its main refinancing rate by 25 basis points to 3.50 percent on Thursday, its second tightening in as many months, but the impact on the dollar was lessened by the widespread assumption the Federal Reserve will hike rates as well next week. \par \par \uc2  In a Reuters poll, all 30 primary dealers forecast that the Fed would raise short-term interest rates by a quarter percentage point on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "But if the consumer price data (on Friday) turns out to be really nasty, we could see some dollar-selling and U.S. stocks will likely get hit," the first dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled on consumer price index estimated, on average, that it rose 0.4 percent in February and that core CPI, which excludes food and energy, rose 0.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  The euro was supported by mild speculation that the ECB may choose to raise interest rates when it next meets on March 30. \par \par \uc2  Economists said that even after Thursday's quarter-point rate rise, monetary policy remained too accommodative, although many still predicted that the next hike will come in May. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0646 GMT.  All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close \par \par \uc2  at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   16 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9707   0.9713   -0.06    -3.60   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      105.85   105.50   +0.33    +3.56   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.78   102.49   +0.28    -0.31   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6588   1.6589   -0.01    +4.31   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5752   1.5763   -0.07    -2.62   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4705   1.4725   -0.14    +1.73   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6110   0.6110   +0.00    -6.90   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6108   1.6120   -0.07    +0.45   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6154   0.6157   -0.05    -1.36   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0646 GMT.  All data taken from\par \f28 \par 