\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Hoist Dlr Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Continuing daily checks by financial authorities on fund repatriations by Japanese investors made fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pervasive Friday in Asia, pushing the dollar higher against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stayed almost flat against the euro as the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tightening of policy Thursday underpinned the euro's down side. \par \par \uc2  Though the repatriation of dollar-denominated assets by Japanese institutional investors' prior to the fiscal-year end has almost peaked, daily checks by Japanese financial authorities on the volume of planned repatriations still continued Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The routine query, proof that Finance Ministry and Bank of Japan are ready to step in as needed, has solidified fears of a new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they noted. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the daily checks continue, players short of dollars can buy them without worrying about losses," said a senior dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Such buyers Friday were mostly Japanese life insurance companies and importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A near-500 point surge of the Dow Jones Industrial Average overnight also helped the dollar advance against the yen, the dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The DJIA's big jump above the 10000-point level has made the dollar attractive to some traders," said Minoru Shioiri, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Nippon Credit Bank. \par \par \uc2  The index closed Thursday in New York at 10630.60, up 499.19 point from the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, however, met active selling above Y106.00 from Japanese exporters and U.S. and European short-term investment funds, paring some of its gains. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y105.89, above Y105.59 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.52 late Thursday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9698, lower than $0.9708 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $0.9690 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision Thursday to tighten its credit didn't help push the euro up against the dollar and yen, but provided support to its downside, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB's suggestion that the move was partly aimed at upshoring the euro has made traders reluctant to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar and yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Since the ECB had been widely expected to raise its refinancing rate within the month, if not yesterday, it didn't have the force to push the euro up. But it is at least providing support on the downside," said Shuji Takano, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN AMRO Bank. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key refinancing rate by 25 basis point to 3.5% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Downward pressure on the dollar/yen from Japanese investors' dollar-denominated asset repatriations is expected to gradually subside next week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Repatriations appeared to peak Wednesday, when the Bank of Japan stepped in to support the dollar vigorously, some dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "One big life insurance company, for instance, had to sell $3 billion alone on that day. That seems to be why the BOJ had to take action on that day and such large-scale repatriation is unlikely in coming weeks," said the senior Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  As such, many traders expect the dollar to be range-bound between Y104.50 and Y106.50 next week. \par \par \uc2  Although the U.S. Federal Reserve Board is expected to tighten monetary policy again in its policy-setting Federal Open Market Committee meeting scheduled next Tuesday, the tightening has already been factored into the trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The tightening has long been expected. Dollar/yen moves will probably be calm next week," said Nippon Credit Bank's Shioiri. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y102.69, up from Y102.50 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y102.25 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5740, down from $1.5753 in New York but higher than $1.5728 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Takeshi Takeuchi; 813-5255-2934; takeshi.takeuchi@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3h01guj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
