\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro benefits as conspiracy theories abound. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wayne Cole \par \uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 08:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 16 (Reuters) - The euro won a rare lift on Thursday as the market's imagination worked overtime ahead of a key European monetary policy meeting later in the ay. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a listless session had been livened by a spate of conspiracy theories, the favourite being that the Bank of Japan was ready to capitalise on a possible rate hike from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the euro up. \par \par \uc2  The talk was fuelled by a late burst of euro buying from a circle of Japanese banks that some suspected might have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And it did help lift the euro to the day's high at 102.63 yen compared with 101.73 in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders even reported whispers the Bank of England would join the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push sterling down against the euro. \par \par \uc2  And the whole tale was embellished with the suspicion that because Hurihiko Kuroda, the Japanese Finance Ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, happened to have been in France for an OECD meeting, he must have met someone from the ECB to chat on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Yes, I suppose if the ECB does hike, and that's far from a foregone conclusion, it could be seen as a wondow of opportunity for the BOJ," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But to suggest that the ECB or the BoE would join in is sheer fantasy. That's someone talking their book," he added. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the market was tense enough that the euro did rise on the dollar to $0.9691 from $0.9672. \par \par \uc2  That was no help to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was idling at 105.64 yen from 105.64 late in New York. \par \par \uc2  And both the euro and the dollar remained short of Wednesday's post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs of 102.95 and 106.25 yen, a sobering performance given dealers estimated the BOJ had bought at least $5 to $6 billion on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders did note say the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen during European hours last week, but suspected it was only because it believed the ECB to be unwilling to act on their behalf. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa flatly denied that Japan would ask for ECB assistance, saying that action in Tokyo alone had been effective. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, analysts noted that the ECB had repeatedly ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone. In December, ECB President Wim Duisenberg stated the bank would never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the yen without the participation of the Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  And there was absolutely no sign of the U.S. agreeing to weaken the yen so Japan could be even more competitive. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, U.S. trade data out on Wednesday showed the current account deficit blew out to a record $99.8 billion in the fourth quarter. The full year shortfall ballooned 54 percent to $338 billion or 3.8 percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  "I can just see the Treasury agreeing to push the yen lower so Japan can export more to the States," said a U.S. bank dealer with more than a small trace of sarcasm. \par \par \uc2  And even if the ECB were to hike rates, analysts doubted it would provide lasting support to the euro, particularly when it came to the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Rate differentials haven't been a big determinant for the yen for a long time," Marshall Gittler, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk at Bank of America in Hong Kong, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  He pointed out that the opposite had been the case in recent time, with the yen actually rising when yield differentials widened against Japan. \par \par \uc2  Instead, traders were focused on talk Japanese institutions had a real need to hedge their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure ahead of the looming fiscal year-end and were praying for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give them better levels to sell. \par \par \uc2  "There's supposed to be a wall of offers from these guys up above 103.00 on the euro and 106.30 on the dollar," said the U.S. bank dealer. "Even if the ECB does hike and the BOJ does step in, we still can't see the euro getting much higher." ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8584 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3g04jjc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
