\par\par \b \uc2  Euro pulls back vs yen as talk of BOJ action fades. \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 08:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0655 GMT - Euro eases a bit against yen and dollar, as market fails to find any concrete evidence of rumoured Bank of Japan buying of euros against yen. - Dealers detected large-lot bids from some Japanese institutional investors, which may have been taken as BOJ buying of euro for yen. - Speculation was rife that MOF's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Haruhiko Kuroda, who just returned from an OECD meeting in France, may have met ECB officials to discuss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . - Euro\tab \tab \tab buoyed by speculation that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would raise interest rates later in the day. - Market talk centres on possible BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if ECB decides to raise key interest rates, although many dealers sceptical as Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Wednesday Tokyo has not asked ECB to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . - Euro now at 102.35/50 yen, having been up to a high of 102.63 yen, compared with 101.73 yen in late U.S. on Wednesday. - Against dollar, it was $0.9697/03 vs $0.9672 in late U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8478 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3g04jam\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
