\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro struggles to break free ahead of ECB. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 16 (Reuters) - The euro was chirpy but unable to break above the top of the past fortnight's range against the dollar on Thursday, with nerves frayed ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-setting meeting later. \par \par \uc2  Traders and analysts said a 25 basis point rate hike was discounted by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, even though only 19 of 44 economists polled by Reuters earlier this week expected a hike. \par \par \uc2  The euro would benefit from a larger than expected rise of 50 basis points, traders said. But the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses would be contained even if the ECB kept rates steady, on the promise of riches to come, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The markets have more or less fully discounted 25 basis points," said Paul Lambert, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London. "But if the ECB does not raise rates, the market will move to expect 25 basis points at the next meeting, and the euro's fall will be limited." \par \par \uc2  The ECB raised its refinancing rate by 25 basis points to 3.25 percent on February 3. It will make its statement on interest rates at 1245 GMT, but will not hold a news conference. \par \par \uc2  The euro hugged the day's high around $0.97 during the European morning, against recent highs around $0.9730 set on Monday. \par \par \uc2  It found support from stronger-than-expected German data, released earlier on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Wholesale prices rose 1.1 percent in February from January, and rose 5.7 percent on the year, the strongest annual increase since September, 1989. \par \par \uc2  "Eurozone data has been surprisingly strong recently and the probability we are going to see a rate hike is higher," said Alexander Nagel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is slightly firmer because today people are putting on trades, in case the ECB surprises with a 50 basis point rate hike. Twenty-five basis points is the consensus and 50 basis points is more likely than nothing." \par \par \uc2  FEAR OF BOJ RECEDES IN EUROPE \par \par \uc2  In Asia, traders said a bout of euro buying against the yen by Japanese banks sparked speculation the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may capitalise on a possible ECB tightening by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But European traders said this was an unlikely scenario. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the euro fell below 102 yen, nearly one yen below the day's high, and the dollar slipped towards 105 yen, as traders said recent experience indicated the BOJ preferred not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in European trading hours. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ, which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least 16 times since June, 1999, to curb the yen's industry-crippling strength, bought about $5 billion to $6 billion worth of dollars for yen on Wednesday, traders in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  But on Wednesday, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa flatly denied that Japan would ask for ECB assistance, saying that action in Tokyo alone had been effective. \par \par \uc2  Japan's economy remains weak and needs to be supported by a further easing of monetary conditions by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Hideyuki Aizawa, the head of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party's financial affairs panel, told Reuters on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling shed a quarter cent against the dollar and dropped to two-week lows against the euro after a larger-than-expected 1.2 percent drop in British retail sales in February, which dampened expectations of higher interest rates anytime soon. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sterling fell to a low for the day just below $1.57\tab  , against a seven-month low of $1.5677 set on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/sterling reached a peak of 61.79 pence, more than three percent above record lows of 59.80 pence set on January 31.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3g04ixr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
