\par\par \b \uc2  Euro Disappoints Bulls; Fails To React To ECB Rate Hike \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON -(Dow Jones)- Euro bulls hoping for a lift from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday were disappointed after a quarter-percentage-point rate increase failed to rally the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1245 GMT, the ECB raised its benchmark short-term interest rate to 3.50% from 3.25%, defying bank-watchers who had discounted a change in monetary policy because the ECB didn't have a press conference on its schedule Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Around 1300 GMT, the euro was at $0.9668, down slightly from $0.9685 just before the rate announcement. The euro was trading at $0.9690 late in Asia and $0.9678 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at Y101.89, down from Y102.12 before the rate move. The euro was at Y102.25 in Asia and Y102.22 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, meanwhile, was at Y105.36, down from Y105.52 late in Asia and Y105.62 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro's failure to rally Thursday will probably make an upward breakout even more difficult for the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar and yen in the short to medium term. European traders had said a break of $0.9700 was crucial in order for the euro to be able to stage an assault on resistance expected around $0.9730. \par \par \uc2  The euro's reaction may also increase speculation about Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro has hit a succession of all-time lows against the yen in recent sessions as fiscal year-end repatriation and a host of other factors boost yen buying. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the past two weeks to keep the yen from appreciating too rapidly against the dollar and euro. With the euro back under Y102.00, traders are likely to be cautious about selling the euro too aggressively. \par \par \uc2  The euro could face more selling pressure in New York after the release of U.S. economic data later Thursday. Producer prices for February are scheduled for release at 1330 GMT, and economists are expecting a strong showing. \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3g01fyw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
