\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Japan Fund Repatriation Drags Dlr Down Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 06:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday proved not much of a help to the dollar against the yen Thursday, as Japanese investors continued to sell dollars for yen to repatriate their dollar assets ahead of the fiscal year-end. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slightly weakened against the euro due to technical selling ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had only tenuous after-effects in Thursday's Asian trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutional investors sold dollars at the high-Y105 levels to repatriate their dollar-denominated assets for their fiscal-year end bookclosing. Japanese exporters also sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the same levels on sentiment that Wednesday's BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to support the dollar above Y106.00, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese interbank players' dollar buying on dips gave the dollar minimal support at a little below Y105.50, they noted. \par \par \uc2  "The highest level the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday was at Y106.25 to the dollar. But the dollar couldn't hold above Y106.00 even one night," said a senior Tokyo-based dealer at a U.S. bank. "All the BOJ's action could do was to renew the fear of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  below Y105.00." \par \par \uc2  But even this renewed fear may not prevent the dollar from falling, albeit temporarily, below Y105.00 over the coming weeks, some dealers said. Japanese investors are expected to step up their repatriation during the period, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Repatriation will create a glut of dollars. It's getting harder for the dollar to stay above Y105.00," said Shuji Takano, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN AMRO Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y105.52, below Y105.62 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y104.91 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9690, higher than $0.9678 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9669 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters have recently begun lowering levels of dollar-selling for the hedging purpose, creating additional downward pressures on the dollar against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  These exporters haven't finished hedging their business transactions for the April-June period. After having seen that the dollar is top-heavy around Y106.00, they started hedge-selling below that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Repatriation and hedge-selling are likely to push the dollar to as low as Y103.80 at one point in the coming weeks," said Ryuichi Takami, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  A majority of market players expect the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave its policy unchanged at its meeting to be held later in the day. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB is likely to postpone a credit tightening to the next meeting on March 30. There is little reason to hurry in squeezing credit," said ABN AMRO's Takano. \par \par \uc2  Even if the bank surprises the market by raising interest rates Thursday, the effect on the euro would likely be limited, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "If the margin of raise is 25 basis points, the euro could rise to $0.9800 and to Y104.00. But their rise is likely to be short-lived since the market has been expecting the rate rise, if not today, at the next meeting," said Takami. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y102.25, up from Y102.22 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y101.44 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5728, down from $1.5745 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Takeshi Takeuchi; 813-5255-2929; takeshi.takeuchi@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3g01f96\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
