\par\par \b \uc2  Ex-MOF Utsumi: Dlr Fall Below Y105 Bad For  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Econ \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 06:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The latest rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted by Japanese monetary authorities to buoy the dollar have been very effective, Keio University professor Makoto Utsumi said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Dow Jones Newswires, the former vice finance minister for international affairs said, "Both \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were very effective even though they were unilateral." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on March 8 and 15, buying dollars for yen and helping to boost the dollar and the euro against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both days. \par \par \uc2  At 0400 GMT Thursday, the dollar was trading at Y105.48, and the euro was trading at Y101.85. \par \par \uc2  "A fall of the dollar below Y105.00 would be damaging to Japan's economy. An excessively strong yen would cast a shadow on the economic recovery. That's why the BOJ and MOF don't want an excessively strong yen prematurely," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi also pointed out that the Finance Ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance has not changed and will remain unchanged going forward. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Japan's monetary authorities could overcome the market forces currently driving the yen up, Utsumi said "I don't believe the market forces pushing down the dollar are that strong." \par \par \uc2  He added that any future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out by the BOJ would be solo in nature, as the likelihood of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the U.S. Federal Reserve is extremely slim. \par \par \uc2  During the next six months, Utsumi said he foresees the dollar trading in a range of Y105 to Y115. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the dollar will move out of a Y105-Y115 range over the next six months," he said. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the recent sharp fall of the euro against the yen, Utsumi said, "Japanese investors have been hurt by the euro's weakness and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't act at all." \par \par \uc2  Utsumi said that Japanese investors' book-value rate of the euro-yen, on average, is around Y130. \par \par \uc2  "Given the 15% rule, a rate of Y108-Y110 would be the limit for investors not to realize \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses. Now, it's Y102-Y103, so investors wish to sell euro paper and euro-yen," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese law requires life insurance companies here to report losses in the value of assets caused by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations when the asset prices at the closing date of March 31 are lower by 15% or more than the original purchase prices. \par \par \uc2  "If the ECB wants a more stable euro, (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would have been good. But, it appears that ECB doesn't want to do this. It is unfortunate," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  Should the euro continue its weak trend, Utsumi said the upcoming meeting of finance ministers from the Group of Seven major industrialized nations is highly likely to discuss this issue. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi said Japan's economy is clearly improving despite the past two quarters of negative growth. \par \par \uc2  "There are some defects in Japan's gross domestic product data," he said. "For example, investment in software is not considered. Also, measurement of private consumption is very problematic." \par \par \uc2  Utsumi pointed out that the nation's economy is recovering as confidence improves among business leaders, managers, and investors and as economic indicators turn positive. \par \par \uc2  "Employment data such as job offers are in an upward trend, overtime in the manufacturing sector is increasing, registration of new passenger cars is picking up, and sales of apartments in the metropolitan area are rising," Utsumi said, adding that recent trends in machinery orders are very positive along with the index of producer inventories. \par \par \uc2  "I think we're beginning to see some signs of a self-sustained economic recovery," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui; 813-5255-2929; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3g01f83\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
