\par\par \b \uc2  Yen keeps bullish tone,euro recovery falters. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 867 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 04:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 15 (Reuters) - The euro faltered after a rebound against the yen and appeared to be again stuck in a downtrend by midday in Tokyo on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  It was pulled down by selling interest among Japanese investors that helped underscore the yen's bullish tone. \par \par \uc2  The euro had hit a lifetime low of 100.60 yen overnight. It recovered to as high around 101.90 yen at one stage during the morning then ebbed again towards midday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also softer against the yen falling below 105.00 yen. The greenback had hit a low of 104.60 yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  But movements remained lacklustre as lingering concerns of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hindered dealers from aggressively testing lows. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at 101.350/50 yen compared with 101.70 yen in late U.S. trade on Tuesday, while the dollar was at 104.92/5.02 yen against 105.20 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar has been declining for so many days, it wouldn't be surprising to see a turnaround. But the market is just waiting to sell on such a rebound," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer said: "Not many (dollar) shorts are building up...so it makes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  difficult." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting as the government's agent, last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy dollars and euros for yen on March 8. \par \par \uc2  The market failed to heed warnings on Wednesday from Vice Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui, who said Japan would take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if moves were volatile. \par \par \uc2  The euro's rebound above 101 yen from overnight lows seemed to slightly ease market tensions about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  And with seasonal selling interest from Japanese investors in the short run, especially in yen cross trades, fund flows seemed to favour the yen. \par \par \uc2  On the stock market, the benchmark Nikkei average continued to decline, ending the morning session down 1.21 percent or 230.79 points at 18,911.05. \par \par \uc2  But it continued to have little impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Rather, there was talk that a large U.S. mutual fund was seeking to buy Nikkei shares on dips and would have to raise yen as the fund operated outside of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was pressured against the dollar after rising to around $0.9691 overnight after the Nasdaq index declined by more than four percent. \par \par \uc2  That helped push the euro up against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro's gains were further fuelled by speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise key interest rates at its governing council meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank directorate member Edgar Meister said on Tuesday that the ECB had primed financial markets well to expect an interest rate increase and that the only question now remaining was timing. \par \par \uc2  "There had been speculation earlier this week but Meister's remarks were the nail in the coffin. The market is now factoring in a 25 basis point hike on Thursday," the trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The euro also received a lift in the morning after Bank of England Monetary Policy Committee member Willem Buiter said that the euro's weakness had not been a problem until recently. \par \par \uc2  "The recent depreciation of the euro, together with (higher) oil prices, provides a real threat to the (ECB) inflation target rate," said Buiter. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0306 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   14 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9663   0.9680   -0.18    -4.04   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      104.90   105.20   -0.29    +2.63   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     101.39   101.70   -0.30    -1.66   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6670   1.6640   +0.18    +4.83   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5741   1.5770   -0.18    -2.69   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4628   1.4645   -0.12    +1.20   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6134   0.6145   -0.18    -6.54   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6111   1.6117   -0.04    +0.47   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6130   0.6134   -0.07    -1.75   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0306 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   14 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9663   0.9680   -0.18    -4.04   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      104.90   105.20   -0.29    +2.63   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     101.39   101.70   -0.30    -1.66   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6670   1.6640   +0.18    +4.83   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5741   1.5770   -0.18    -