\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar leaps vs yen after BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2      By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 907 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 08:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 15 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped against the yen \par \par \uc2  late Wednesday in Tokyo after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2      The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market when the \par \par \uc2  dollar was trading around 104.80/90 yen, dealers said.  The \par \par \uc2  dollar quickly leapt to a high of 105.75 yen, and the BOJ was \par \par \uc2  still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a week ago, selling yen for dollars \par \par \uc2  in an effort to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has \par \par \uc2  appreciated 6.4 percent against the dollar since Feb. 22. \par \par \uc2      At 0615 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 105.58/68 yen, compared \par \par \uc2  with 105.20 yen in late U.S. trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar gained around one yen. So far the impact of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was limited," Takahiro Ninomiya, manager at Toyo \par \par \uc2  Trust Bank, told Reuters Television. "The BOJ likely wants to \par \par \uc2  prevent the dollar from falling below 104.50 yen before the end \par \par \uc2  of fiscal year" on March 31. \par \par \uc2      Overnight, the Japanese yen muscled to 104.60 yen, and \par \par \uc2  strengthened to a lifetime high of 100.60 versus the euro. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar and the euro have been at sensitive levels, so it \par \par \uc2  was just a matter of a time (until the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," a dealer \par \par \uc2  at a major Japanese city bank said. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the BOJ so far had been seen buying only dollars \par \par \uc2  against the yen, but said buying of euros with yen is likely \par \par \uc2  during European trading hours. \par \par \uc2      "It is possible that the BOJ will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own during \par \par \uc2  European hours," Ninomiya said. \par \par \uc2      The euro rose to a high of 102.57 yen, compared with 101.70 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen in late U.S. trade. The euro\tab   was slightly easier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar, standing at $0.9673/75 versus $0.9680 in late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro's downside is supported by speculation that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise key interest rates when its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par governing council meets on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since the BOJ last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on March 8, the yen had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciated 2.6 percent against the dollar. The yen had surged\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since Monday when surprisingly strong capital spending data was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par released, restoring confidence that the economy was clearly on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth path.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ appeared to have spent much more yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying dollars on Wednesday that it did earlier this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, dealers wonder whether the dollar's gains can be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sustained, especially as a large amount of offers exist above 106\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ probably waited to act until yen call\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par options with a strike price of 105.00 yen matured in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par afternoon to make its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more effective. Such options\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par kept the spot rate stuck much of the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the yen's strength versus the Aussie dollar and British\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sterling had weighed on the dollar against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8478\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight, the Japanese yen muscled to 104.60 yen, and strengthened to a lifetime high of 100.60 versus the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The dollar and the euro have been at sensitive levels, so it was just a matter of a time (until the BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )," the bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since the BOJ last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on March 8, the yen had appreciated 2.6 percent against the dollar. The yen had surged since Monday when surprisingly strong capital spending data was released, restoring confidence that the economy was clearly on a growth path.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ appeared to have spent much more yen buying dollars on Wednesday that it did earlier this month. Still, dealers wonder whether the dollar's gains can be sustained, especially as a large amount of offers exist above 106 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The dollar gained around one yen. So far the impact of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was limited," Takahiro Ninomiya, manager at Toyo Trust Bank, told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ likely wants to prevent the dollar from falling below 104.50 yen before the end of fiscal year settlements at the end of the month...but the yen's bias will likely remain on the upside for a while. Japanese customers such as exporters are showing selling interest."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ probably waited to act until yen call options with a strike price of 105.00 yen matured in the afternoon to make its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more effective. Such options kept the spot rate stuck much of the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the yen's strength versus the Aussie dollar and British sterling had weighed on the dollar against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ so far had been seen buying only dollars against the yen, but said buying of euros with yen is likely during European trading hours.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It is possible that the BOJ will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on its own during European hours," Ninomiya said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro also rose to a high of 102.57 yen, compared with 101.70 yen in late U.S. trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   was slightly easier against the dollar, standing at $0.9673/75 versus $0.9680 in late U.S. on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro's downside is supported by speculation that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise key interest rates when its governing council meets on Thursday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8478 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3f04o