\par\par \b \uc2  TOCOM platinum ends mixed as dollar bounces vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 15 (Reuters) - Yen-based platinum futures ended mixed on Wednesday, erasing a large portion of their early losses when the dollar bounced against the yen after \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to the Tokyo Commodity Exchange's (TOCOM) announcement that it will maintain a price freeze on its April-December palladium futures contracts until they expire. The move was in line with expectations, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The major event for today was the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the dollar's bounce against the yen," said a commodity brokerage analyst. \par \par \uc2  "The TOCOM announcement was not surprising, because it was just a continuation of what it has already done. It was within market expectations," he said. \par \par \uc2  Platinum futures ranged from 12 yen per gram lower to four yen higher. Benchmark February ended up four yen at 1,394 yen, rebounding from the day's low of 1,378 yen. \par \par \uc2  Spot platinum was quoted at $479.00/485.00 an ounce at 0700 GMT, against $482.00/$490.00 in late London trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Spot palladium was quoted at $685.00/715.00 an ounce at 0700 GMT, against $680.00/$710.00 in London on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Open interest of platinum futures was 298,954 lots at the end of Tuesday trade, against 303,208 lots on Monday. On Wednesday, TOCOM also announced it would accept new positions for the benchmark February 2001 palladium contract, which had previously been limited to hedging positions. \par \par \uc2  TOCOM said the opening of trade in February palladium futures to non-hedging positions will commence after the Ministry of International Trade and Industry approves revised exchange regulations to tighten open position limits and increase margins. \par \par \uc2  No trading of the benchmark February palladium contract has been reported since it was listed on February 25. \par \par \uc2  Open interest of palladium futures was 40,044 lots at the end of Tuesday trade, against 40,149 lots on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the gold market, futures closed lower as a cautious mood prevailed ahead of next week's British gold auction, traders said. But losses were limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements. \par \par \uc2  Prices ranged from four to 10 yen per gram lower. Benchmark February ended off seven yen at 973 yen. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England will auction some 25 tonnes of gold next Tuesday as the last in the current tranche of sales to reduce its official gold holdings to 300 tonnes from 715 tonnes. \par \par \uc2  Open interest of gold futures was 302,806 lots at the end of Tuesday trade, up from 301,853 lots on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Silver futures ranged from 1.0 yen per 10 grams lower to 1.0 yen higher. Benchmark February ended off 0.2 yen at 168.8 yen. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar leapt to a high of 105.75 yen in late Tokyo trade on Wednesday. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when the dollar was trading around 104.80/90 yen, dealers said. ((Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431 tokyo.commodit.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3f04or9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
