\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen claws back ground as BOJ fears ebb. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 15 (Reuters) - The yen pared losses suffered after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for dollars for the third time this year on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose as high as 106.20 yen and the euro rallied to 103.25 yen in the wake of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action, which took place during Asian hours and was later confirmed by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  While Miyazawa warned the foreign exchanges Japan could take more such action if necessary, the yen clawed back ground during European hours. Analysts said the absence of any further action so far and a feeling the BOJ was going against the tide was responsible for the retracement. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was mildly effective but the market is fairly sceptical and if they don't come in again I suspect we will see dollar/yen retrace just about all the way," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Warburg Dillon Read in London. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ are totally going against the wind in the sense that there is good underlying demand for yen from Japanese investors to hedge some of their exposures." \par \par \uc2  Since the BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 8, the yen had appreciated 2.6 percent against the dollar. Its most recent boost has been since Monday when surprisingly strong capital spending data was released, restoring confidence that the economy was on a growth path. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least 16 times since June 1999. \par \par \uc2  Bankers in Tokyo had spotted the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars for yen when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was languishing at 104.80/90 yen. That lifted the dollar to a high of 105.75 yen and the BOJ was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level as well. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was within 1/2 yen of its 106.20 post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  high by 1021 GMT, up more than one percent from Tuesday's 104.55 six-week low. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like they want to establish 105 as a level that they do not want to see breached. But it might be difficult because the capital expenditure figures, part of Monday's GDP figures, are showing some hint of possible self-sustained recovery in Japan, which increases confidence about the yen," said Joanne Collins, senior economist at Daiwa SBCM Europe in London. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa also said he had not asked the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  Market disappointment on the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity to follow up the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was putting pressure on euro/yen which had fallen 1-1/4 yen from its 103.25 day's peak, but was still around 1.5 percent above record lows around 100.50 set a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  EURO CONSILIDATION VS DOLLAR CONTINUES \par \par \uc2  The euro's decline against the yen had dragged euro/dollar to its day's lows around $0.9640, but it was still towards the top of its recent $0.9519/0.9728 range. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the euro had gleaned some support against the dollar after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was knocked by a four percent fall in the Nasdaq composite index on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market would watch early U.S. stock market trading and any fall there could put upward pressure on euro/dollar. \par \par \uc2  The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also expected to be underpinned by persistent market speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might raise its 3.25 percent refinancing rate at Thursday's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, sterling was holding above Tuesday's $1.5677 seven-month low, helped in part by stronger-than-expected British average earnings data which rose 5.9 percent in the three months to January, its highest since July 1992. \par \par \uc2  "Today's data will certainly maintain risk that the MPC (Monetary Policy Committee) may feel the compulsion to raise rates again, so sterling is reasonably well supported," said Crise at Warburg Dillon Read. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3f04kut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
