\par\par \b \uc2  Miyazawa -  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened \highlight\uc2  on yen, may do so again. \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 15 (Reuters) - Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed on Wednesday that Japan had sold yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and said the authorities may do so again if needed. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, I've been told we took action," Miyazawa told a regular news conference when asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market talk that Tokyo sold yen for dollars to halt the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise after it hit six-week highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Depending on the circumstances, we may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  a bit more," he said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said it would be troublesome to have \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market disruptions just as the world's second-biggest economy "shows unmistakable signs of getting back on a growth track". \par \par \uc2  But Japan so far is acting alone to curb the yen's rise, Miyazawa said, saying Tokyo has not asked the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  "We have not asked the ECB to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on our behalf," Miyazawa said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Tokyo market have been effective. \par \par \uc2  "If necessary we will do that (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through other central banks), but as long as that is not the case, I think it's enough to act in the Tokyo market." \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa declined comment on specific exchange rates but said it was unfavourable for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move too much in either direction and that Japan stood ready to act in response to disruptive movements. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said there were uncertain factors looming over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, such as fund flows at the end of the Japanese fiscal year to March 31 and uncertainty about U.S. and European interest rate moves. \par \par \uc2  "Given such factors, we must act pre-emptively to defend (market stability)," he said. ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3f04j7t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
