\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Dollar/yen shines while BOJ wariness reigns. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 15 (Reuters) - The dollar zoomed up against the yen on Wednesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during Asian trading hours a week after its last market action. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed Japan had sold yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday, adding the authorities might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if necessary. \par \par \uc2  He also said he did not want disruptions in the market and said he had not asked the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in London said its remarks forced the yen to backtrack even further amid wariness of possible renewed market action by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  "Once you've got Miyazawa himself saying they might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again you've got to be a bit worried," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in London. "That's what's keeping dollar/yen supported at the moment." \par \par \uc2  Bankers in Tokyo had spotted the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars for yen when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was languishing at 104.80/90 yen JPY=). That lifted the dollar to a high of 105.75 yen and the BOJ was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level as well. \par \par \uc2  By 0815 GMT, the dollar was hugging 106 yen, up more than one percent from the lows seen before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and well above a six-week low of 104.55 it set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen was hovering around 102.50 EURJPY=), looking a little bit shaky despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it had dropped to record lows around 100.50 just a day earlier, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  "The only reason for euro/yen to be supported is the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , otherways it would be a lot lower," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But if the ECB hikes rates tomorrow, this might take us a bit higher in the short-term." \par \par \uc2  Persistent market speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might raise rates at its policy meeting on Thursday were providing some support for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro, which had been initially sold after weak Italian January industrial output data, found a base above the day's lows around $0.9670 EUR=). \par \par \uc2  ANALYSTS QUESTION BOJ ACTION \par \par \uc2  The BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a week ago, selling yen for dollars in an effort to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has appreciated 6.4 percent against the dollar since February 22. \par \par \uc2  Since the BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 8, the yen had appreciated 2.6 percent against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been boosted since Monday when surprisingly strong capital spending data was released, restoring confidence that the economy was on a growth path. \par \par \uc2  Analysts questioned the effectivness of this new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they said that signs that the worst was over for Japan's economy would encourage speculators to bet on the yen again soon. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar has been lifted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they may be fighting a losing battle at the moment," said Joanne Collins, senior economist at Nomura in London. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like they want to establish 105 as a level that they do not want to see breached. But it might be difficult because the capital expenditure figures, part of Monday's GDP figures, are showing some hint of possible self-sustained recovery in Japan, which increases confidence about the yen." \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3f04j1q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
