\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen creeps up despite BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 15:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 15 (Reuters) - The yen rebounded on Wednesday from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength as traders bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was fighting against a tide of optimism about Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  The yen dropped in Asian trading hours after the Bank of Japan on Wednesday sold yen for dollars for the third time this year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action sent the dollar soaring from near six-week lows around 104.80 yen to a high of 106.20 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro also rallied from a trough above the 101 yen level to a peak of 103.25 yen. \par \par \uc2  Despite warnings from Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa that Japan could take more action if necessary to prevent a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from derailing prospects for recovery, the market drove the yen back to its upward track. \par \par \uc2  In early New York dealings, the dollar traded near 105.50 yen and the euro slid below 102 yen to stand little more than one yen from an all-time floor hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously, the market is a little sceptical of the Bank of Japan," said Rick Gomes, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HSBC in New York. \par \par \uc2  "There has been a pretty steady capital inflow into Japan. There seems to be growing positive sentiment, so the BoJ seems to be fighting sentiment at the moment," he said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market would likely push the yen higher but predicted a cautious New York session amid wariness of being caught wrong-footed by further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market was little swayed by data showing U.S. industrial production rose by a softer than expected 0.3 percent in February, with traders gearing up for key U.S. inflation reports on Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  Since the BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 8, the yen had risen 2.6 percent against the dollar. It received a boost on Monday from data pointing to a spike in capital spending in late 1999 even as the overall economy shrank. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Prime Minister Obuchi reinforced the positive tone even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took action, saying Japan's dip into a technical recession in the second half of 1999 was temporary and that growth would be positive this fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said investment capital flows ahead of the Japanese fiscal year-end on March 31 would encourage strong demand for yen over the next couple of weeks. \par \par \uc2  "I think the market perceives there is a turnaround in Japan, and, as long as we continue to see repatriation flows, I think the market will continue to test the will of the BoJ," said Ben Strauss, vice president at Bank Julius Baer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro looked especially vulnerable to further declines and possible speculative attack against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The renewed risk of Japanese investors hedging their euro holdings is undermining euro/yen, which is weighing on euro/dollar," said Michael Lewis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Deutsche Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  In early New York, the euro traded around 96.70 cents, a touch weaker against the dollar from its Tuesday close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro's failure to benefit from wobbles on U.S. equity markets and rising speculation the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may raise its 3.25 percent refinancing rate as soon as Thursday did not bode well for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "A rate hike is already priced into the market," said Julius Baer's Strauss, adding that a rate hike may give the euro a temporary lift at best. \par \par \uc2  "It's a case of market sentiment being so bearish that it overwhelms any positve news," he said, ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212 859 1690)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1408GMT.  All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 14 Mar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9653   0.9680   -0.28   -4.14   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     105.45   105.20   +0.24   +3.17   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    101.83   101.70   +0.13   -1.23   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6678   1.6640   +0.23   +4.88   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5703   1.5770   -0.42   -2.92   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4685   1.4645   +0.27   +1.59   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6130   0.6145   -0.24   -6.60   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6110   1.6117   -0.04   +0.46   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6150   0.6134   +0.26   -1.43   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3f04gjo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
