\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen powers higher against dollar and euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 14 (Reuters) - The yen forged higher on Tuesday breaking to record peaks against the euro and six-week highs against the dollar amid growing confidence that the Japanese economy was on the path to recovery. \par \par \uc2  The market was keen to test Japan's resolve to curb excessive yen strength, amid confidence the recovery was finally becoming self-sustaining despite rhetoric from some Japanese officials that the economy was still fragile. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted yen bulls had gained an upper hand after Monday's Japanese October-December gross domestic product data showed a 4.6 percent pickup in capital spending, even though GDP itself was down for a second consecutive quarter - technically putting the world's second largest economy back in recession. \par \par \uc2  "The natural market inclination is to push the yen higher at the moment," said Stephen Hannah, director of research at IBJ International in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had fallen to as low as 104.72 by 1040 GMT, down more than one yen on the day to its lowest since January 28. The euro was also down more than a yen on the day, setting record lows below 100.90. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said yen strength was likely to continue ahead of the fiscal year end, on March 31, but did not rule out the possibility that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem too sharp a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo earlier in the day, Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, asked for his opinion on the yen strength in the wake of the GDP data, said, "Well, if moves are too rapid, we will act." \par \par \uc2  "The potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is there, but at the moment it might not be that effective," said an analyst at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still pretty bullish with some investment flow into Japan and it may be no more than a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa also said Japan had started on the road to a self-sustaining recovery but later warned that it would be difficult to achieve a 2.0 percent rise in January-March GDP, needed to reach the government's 0.6 percent growth target for the 1999-2000 fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  EURO STRUGGLES TO CAPITALISE ON GAINS \par \par \uc2  The euro was unable hold on to Monday's brief rise to 1-1/2 week highs above $0.97 amid U.S. stock market weakness. It was subdued in a tight range below $0.9650 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The market still hasn't quite got to grips with buying the euro," the Japanese bank analyst said. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq composite index, which the dollar has tracked in recent weeks, fell 2.8 percent on Monday, closing below 5,000. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the euro appeared unable to capitalise on growing speculation the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would raise interest rates at its upcoming governing council meeting on Thursday, rather than at the next meeting on March 30 as had been previously expected. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a 25 basis point rise in euro zone rates might not be sufficient to lift the euro given that the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee was also expected to hike rates next week. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the euro has weakened as much as it has now probably means that if we do see 25 basis points by the ECB is really factored in and it could be a case of almost buy-on-the-rumour and sell-on-the-fact,"said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic advisor at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "The big picture is still one in which the euro is going to struggle." REUTERS. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3e04kyz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
